238
00:07:25,377 --> 00:07:26,679
[Springs up]
Oh, okay!

239
00:07:26,679 --> 00:07:27,660
My arms don't reach.

240
00:07:27,660 --> 00:07:28,487
- Go?
- I'll go now.

241
00:07:28,487 --> 00:07:30,527
DAWN really likes this program now.

242
00:07:30,527 --> 00:07:33,044
[Job satisfaction level: Max]
Dda-dda-dda-dda-dda!

243
00:07:33,044 --> 00:07:34,377
Hey, he's good.

244
00:07:34,377 --> 00:07:37,043
Why is he going down so well…?

245
00:07:37,043 --> 00:07:39,077
[Comfortable as if he's resting his knees]

246
00:07:39,077 --> 00:07:40,577
[Swoosh]
Ugh, DAWN, you're so annoying!

247
00:07:40,577 --> 00:07:41,643
- Whoa!
- Hey!

248
00:07:41,643 --> 00:07:43,244
Why are you enjoying it so much?!

249
00:07:43,244 --> 00:07:44,977
We're way too stable!

250
00:07:44,977 --> 00:07:47,543
[Celebratory dance]
Ddan-ddan-ddan-ddan-ddan!

251
00:07:47,543 --> 00:07:49,892
He's going wild, even dancing!

252
00:07:49,892 --> 00:07:51,777
[A forced smile]
I thought you were a robot or AI.

253
00:07:51,777 --> 00:07:53,098
I'll go right away.

254
00:07:53,098 --> 00:07:54,177
If the flag falls first, you lose.

255
00:07:54,177 --> 00:07:55,370
[His competitive spirit fires up]
Okay.

256
00:07:55,370 --> 00:07:57,377
My arms don't reach over there.

257
00:07:58,009 --> 00:08:00,176
[Bold]
Oh.

258
00:08:00,176 --> 00:08:02,076
[What a man!]
Oh!

259
00:08:03,843 --> 00:08:05,077
That's risky!

260
00:08:05,077 --> 00:08:06,044
- Dig just a little bit, a little!
- DAWN, you have to dig a little bit.

261
00:08:06,044 --> 00:08:07,148
[Proud]
Hey Ji Sung, you're good.

262
00:08:07,148 --> 00:08:07,881
This isn't easy.

263
00:08:07,881 --> 00:08:09,388
- Nothing's uncomfortable, right?
- I'm good, Lee Teuk.

264
00:08:09,388 --> 00:08:10,900
Alright, here we go!
Let's go!

265
00:08:10,900 --> 00:08:12,976
DAWN is super hyped right now.

266
00:08:12,976 --> 00:08:14,810
[Teasing, teasing]
That's when you start losing.

267
00:08:14,810 --> 00:08:17,709
[A man who defies gravity]
Yeah, he's so cool! DAWN!

268
00:08:18,190 --> 00:08:19,376
Oh, he's not really digging.

269
00:08:20,876 --> 00:08:22,276
Oh, what?!

270
00:08:22,276 --> 00:08:23,377
[Barren]
Oh, what?!

271
00:08:23,377 --> 00:08:24,144
- Wow!
- Okay!

272
00:08:24,144 --> 00:08:25,982
- That's right!
- Okay!

273
00:08:25,982 --> 00:08:28,677
- DAWN was born to play this game!
- Ji Sung.

274
00:08:28,677 --> 00:08:30,876
- If we win this time, that flag's gonna fall!
- That's right!

275
00:08:30,876 --> 00:08:32,255
- Endure it just one more time!!!
- Okay!

276
00:08:32,255 --> 00:08:33,987
- Let's go!
- Let's go! Let's go!

277
00:08:34,876 --> 00:08:36,976
Agh… Come here…

278
00:08:37,609 --> 00:08:39,736
[Careful]

279
00:08:39,736 --> 00:08:41,436
[The wind is picking up...!]

280
00:08:42,876 --> 00:08:45,776
[The sea wind suddenly gets strong]

281
00:08:47,966 --> 00:08:48,774
Is it done? Did you do it?

282
00:08:48,774 --> 00:08:51,568
[Nice]
Oof! Hey!

283
00:08:51,568 --> 00:08:52,842
- You have to be gentle now.
- Hey, we're in trouble.

284
00:08:52,842 --> 00:08:53,910
You have to soothe it now.

285
00:08:53,910 --> 00:08:56,012
Ohhhhh!!!

286
00:08:56,012 --> 00:08:57,196
Hurry up, hurry up!

287
00:08:57,196 --> 00:08:59,049
Oh!

288
00:08:59,049 --> 00:09:00,077
[Urgent]
Hurry, hurry, hurry!

289
00:09:00,077 --> 00:09:01,376
- Hurry, hurry, hurry!
- Hurry up, hurry up!

290
00:09:01,376 --> 00:09:02,772
Do it now!!!!!!

291
00:09:02,772 --> 00:09:05,078
[Chaos]
Hurry up!

292
00:09:05,078 --> 00:09:05,879
Hurry, hurry!

293
00:09:05,879 --> 00:09:07,724
This is bad.
Dig to the right side.

294
00:09:07,724 --> 00:09:09,759
- This is no good.
- You have to soothe it, DAWN. Soothe it!

295
00:09:09,759 --> 00:09:10,944
Let's go!

296
00:09:10,944 --> 00:09:11,877
[Determined]
Okay, let's go!

297
00:09:11,877 --> 00:09:13,162
You need to soothe it!

298
00:09:13,162 --> 00:09:14,576
He's suddenly putting on a show!

299
00:09:14,576 --> 00:09:15,498
[Show effect: None whatsoever]

300
00:09:15,498 --> 00:09:17,386
He's suddenly putting on a show.

301
00:09:17,386 --> 00:09:18,878
Easy, easy.

302
00:09:18,878 --> 00:09:20,272
Just a little bit.

303
00:09:20,272 --> 00:09:21,404
Wow, but this…

304
00:09:21,404 --> 00:09:23,457
It won't fall over after that?

305
00:09:23,457 --> 00:09:24,817
[Scratch, scratch, scratch]
Pull?

306
00:09:24,817 --> 00:09:25,577
Should we pull?

307
00:09:25,577 --> 00:09:27,443
- Oh, so annoying.
- Oh, he's doing more.

308
00:09:27,443 --> 00:09:28,311
[Scratch, scratch, scratch]
Oh, so annoying.

309
00:09:28,311 --> 00:09:29,430
He's doing all that he can.

310
00:09:29,430 --> 00:09:31,214
That's right!

311
00:09:31,214 --> 00:09:32,880
- Wow!!
- Oh!!

312
00:09:33,409 --> 00:09:34,810
[After excitedly going back up]

313
00:09:34,810 --> 00:09:37,077
[Plop]
Wow!!

314
00:09:37,077 --> 00:09:39,789
Nice! We won!!

315
00:09:39,789 --> 00:09:41,147
Does that mean we lost...?

316
00:09:41,147 --> 00:09:43,110
The wind was
blowing way too hard.

317
00:09:43,110 --> 00:09:43,977
Nice!

318
00:09:43,977 --> 00:09:45,377
[R1: Team Johnny, WIN]
Ji Sung, great job!

319
00:09:45,377 --> 00:09:47,077
- Good job!
- Oh, but… Oh…

320
00:09:47,077 --> 00:09:48,477
Ji Sung, pick the ramyun!

321
00:09:48,477 --> 00:09:49,878
Choose whatever you want to eat!

322
00:09:49,878 --> 00:09:51,510
- You said you wanted Omori, right?
- Pick what you want!

323
00:09:51,510 --> 00:09:53,790
[Our Ji Sung, choose whatever you want]
I want either Shin Ramyun or Buldak.

324
00:09:53,790 --> 00:09:55,771
[A happy dilemma]
It's finally looking up for Ji Sung!

325
00:09:55,771 --> 00:09:57,272
Oh, thank goodness!

326
00:09:57,272 --> 00:09:58,481
There's almost only one of each.

327
00:09:58,481 --> 00:10:00,277
[Ji Sung's pick!]
There's only one of these.

328
00:10:00,277 --> 00:10:02,344
[The one and only jjajang ramyun]
Oh, good call with Chapagetti.

329
00:10:02,344 --> 00:10:03,810
Oh, you grabbed the jjajang ramyun?

330
00:10:03,810 --> 00:10:05,773
[Jealous]
I really wanted to eat that one.

331
00:10:05,773 --> 00:10:07,280
[Proud]
I really wanted to eat that.

332
00:10:07,280 --> 00:10:08,709
There's only one of those.

333
00:10:08,709 --> 00:10:10,276
- What should we do?
- Let's practice once?

334
00:10:10,276 --> 00:10:11,612
[Next on the offense: Yo Han practices too]
Go down a bit.

335
00:10:11,612 --> 00:10:12,972
[Opal Guy's first time holding the rope]
You just gotta let it go.

336
00:10:12,972 --> 00:10:14,023
No, I'm not using my strength yet.

337
00:10:14,023 --> 00:10:14,877
- You don't have to.
- Oh really?

338
00:10:14,877 --> 00:10:16,977
[Trembling]
Who's playing next? Oh, Yo Han?

339
00:10:16,977 --> 00:10:18,177
[Wobbling]
Uh, oh!

340
00:10:18,177 --> 00:10:19,382
I'm done digging!

341
00:10:19,382 --> 00:10:21,309
It feels like
I'm doing this alone.

342
00:10:21,309 --> 00:10:23,229
This guy…!
What's with this guy?

343
00:10:23,229 --> 00:10:25,261
[Too light to help when it's needed]
Why is he being pulled forward?

344
00:10:25,261 --> 00:10:26,477
Why is he getting pulled down?

345
00:10:26,477 --> 00:10:27,577
Oh, I'm up against Yo Han.

346
00:10:27,577 --> 00:10:29,777
- I feel like Yo Han will be good.
- Is it safe?

347
00:10:29,777 --> 00:10:31,210
I'm good even if I die!

348
00:10:31,210 --> 00:10:33,677
[Round 2: Yo Han VS Lee Teuk]
- "Unwavering Trust", Round 2 will begin! - Let's go!

349
00:10:33,677 --> 00:10:34,855
[Taekwondo Kid is on the move]
When I say to pull him up,

350
00:10:34,855 --> 00:10:35,961
- just stand your ground.
- I'll get started!

351
00:10:35,961 --> 00:10:36,880
Go, go!

352
00:10:36,880 --> 00:10:38,681
Hey, let go a bit, just a little.

353
00:10:38,681 --> 00:10:39,809
Let go more, more.

354
00:10:39,809 --> 00:10:42,776
[Core muscles trained by Taekwondo]
That's right, we're holding on well.

355
00:10:42,776 --> 00:10:43,916
He didn't dig much on this side.

356
00:10:43,916 --> 00:10:44,867
Yeah.

357
00:10:44,867 --> 00:10:46,577
[Relaxed]
Yes, that's it for now.

358
00:10:46,577 --> 00:10:47,976
That's it.

359
00:10:47,976 --> 00:10:49,059
[Sliding]
Hey, Lee Teuk, Lee Teuk!

360
00:10:49,059 --> 00:10:50,509
- Tell us when you're gonna go!
- Oh, got it, got it.

361
00:10:50,509 --> 00:10:51,695
[Still getting ready in the back]

362
00:10:51,695 --> 00:10:53,529
[Charging in]
Oh, Lee Teuk. Tell us when you're gonna go!

363
00:10:53,529 --> 00:10:55,277
[It would've been hilarious if he fell]
You gotta tell us before you go.

364
00:10:55,277 --> 00:10:56,510
I feel rushed.

365
00:10:56,510 --> 00:10:58,452
- Let's go!
- Hold it like this.

366
00:10:58,452 --> 00:10:59,810
Using the sneaky-sneak method!

367
00:10:59,810 --> 00:11:01,504
[Recklessly scooping away the sand]

368
00:11:01,504 --> 00:11:02,462
Up!

369
00:11:02,462 --> 00:11:03,777
Oh, okay.

370
00:11:03,777 --> 00:11:06,244
We're all getting the hang of this!

371
00:11:06,244 --> 00:11:08,678
(Sabotage in action)
Hey, straighten your back, straighten your back!

372
00:11:08,678 --> 00:11:09,777
Should we lift you up?

373
00:11:09,777 --> 00:11:12,365
Yes, I think you can lift me up!

374
00:11:12,365 --> 00:11:13,985
Wow, this is hard.

375
00:11:13,985 --> 00:11:15,477
Wow, you did that well.

376
00:11:15,477 --> 00:11:17,409
[The sand thinned out nicely]
Slowly, slowly.

377
00:11:19,276 --> 00:11:21,177
[Crumbling down]

378
00:11:21,177 --> 00:11:23,226
- Lee Teuk!
- Oh…!

379
00:11:23,226 --> 00:11:24,477
I got this!

380
00:11:24,477 --> 00:11:25,398
Up!

381
00:11:25,398 --> 00:11:26,277
Come on!

382
00:11:26,277 --> 00:11:27,844
Let's hurry up!
We need to do this quickly!

383
00:11:27,844 --> 00:11:28,884
We won this, we won this!

384
00:11:28,884 --> 00:11:30,277
Go down, go all the way down.

385
00:11:30,277 --> 00:11:32,984
[Let's just get through this…!]
Go down, go all the way down.

386
00:11:34,191 --> 00:11:35,758
Wait, you have
to use the other hand.

387
00:11:35,758 --> 00:11:37,440
Use both hands!

388
00:11:37,440 --> 00:11:39,144
- Wow, he's heavy.
- Wow, but…

389
00:11:39,144 --> 00:11:40,944
- Oh, he's doing well.
- Ohhh…!

390
00:11:40,944 --> 00:11:41,777
Ohhh!!!

391
00:11:41,777 --> 00:11:42,991
- Are you done?
- Wait!

392
00:11:42,991 --> 00:11:43,647
It's moving, it's moving!

393
00:11:43,647 --> 00:11:45,776
[Flag flaps wildly]
Wait, it's moving!

394
00:11:45,776 --> 00:11:47,676
[Wobbling]
Oh, wait!!!

395
00:11:47,676 --> 00:11:50,476
[Will Team Johnny win a second time?]
Oh, wait!!!

396
00:11:50,476 --> 00:11:51,976
[Desperate]
Oh, wait!!!

397
00:11:51,976 --> 00:11:53,575
(I'm going)
Agh!!

398
00:11:53,575 --> 00:11:55,677
[R2: Team Johnny wins]
We won!

399
00:11:55,677 --> 00:11:57,777
- What are you doing?!
- No, like, this..! This…!

400
00:11:57,777 --> 00:11:59,510
[Going crazy over how unfair it feels]
No, like, this..! This…!

401
00:11:59,510 --> 00:12:01,044
Hey! You little punk!

402
00:12:01,044 --> 00:12:02,177
[Lee Teuk's pick]
What are Koreans all about?

403
00:12:02,177 --> 00:12:03,533
[A Korean favorite, Kimchi stew ramyun]
Kimchi!

404
00:12:03,533 --> 00:12:05,376
- They're taking all the good stuff!
- That's the tastiest one there!

405
00:12:05,376 --> 00:12:06,977
[Now it's a battle of pride]
The ramyun isn't important here.

406
00:12:06,977 --> 00:12:08,576
We have to win this one.

407
00:12:08,576 --> 00:12:11,076
[The strongest players of each team face off]

408
00:12:11,576 --> 00:12:13,810
Can you loosen this up for me…?

409
00:12:13,810 --> 00:12:15,676
[Embarrassed]
Why is this so small!!

410
00:12:15,676 --> 00:12:18,344
Yo Han was heavy too…
We'll be okay, right…?

411
00:12:18,344 --> 00:12:20,249
- Can you try pulling me up?
- Of course.

412
00:12:20,249 --> 00:12:22,131
- I'll just try it from here.
- Yes, yes.

413
00:12:22,131 --> 00:12:23,576
- Go down?
- Yes.

414
00:12:23,576 --> 00:12:25,743
[Wobbling]
Oh, sorry! Hey, hey!

415
00:12:25,743 --> 00:12:27,177
You can't just pull right away!

416
00:12:27,177 --> 00:12:28,591
- You have to let me go down a bit!
- Sorry, sorry.

417
00:12:28,591 --> 00:12:29,552
Yes, Shin Dong!

418
00:12:29,552 --> 00:12:30,944
[Excessive tension]

419
00:12:30,944 --> 00:12:32,471
[and tremendous distrust]
I was too nervous!

420
00:12:32,471 --> 00:12:33,844
- Go?
- Yes.

421
00:12:33,844 --> 00:12:35,977
- Lower me more!
- You have to let go a bit more.

422
00:12:35,977 --> 00:12:37,366
- Lower me more!
- Let go a bit more, let go!

423
00:12:37,366 --> 00:12:38,776
Lower me more…

424
00:12:38,776 --> 00:12:40,077
Hold on...!

425
00:12:40,077 --> 00:12:42,046
Shin Dong… Shin Dong…!

426
00:12:42,046 --> 00:12:42,977
Let's just pull him up!

427
00:12:42,977 --> 00:12:44,477
[Doesn't know what happened]
Oh, it's working! It was fine.

428
00:12:44,477 --> 00:12:45,510
- Shin Dong, seriously…
- Are you okay?

429
00:12:45,510 --> 00:12:47,844
I don't think
I can do it twice!

430
00:12:47,844 --> 00:12:50,010
[Shin Dong is too heavy for me…]
I don't think I can do it twice.

431
00:12:50,010 --> 00:12:52,882
[Chaos here too]
Oh, hey! He's too heavy! Oof.

432
00:12:52,882 --> 00:12:54,317
[Just endure this round and you'll win!]
We have to finish it on the first try!

433
00:12:54,317 --> 00:12:55,317
If we endure it, we'll win!

434
00:12:55,317 --> 00:12:56,777
Hey, wait a sec...!

435
00:12:56,777 --> 00:12:58,777
[When's the next round gonna start…?]
Tell us before you go down!

436
00:12:58,777 --> 00:13:00,577
You're heavy right now!

437
00:13:00,577 --> 00:13:03,409
[Intense practice]
Please lower him a little bit.

438
00:13:03,409 --> 00:13:05,009
[Trembling]

439
00:13:05,009 --> 00:13:07,376
[Rapid aging]

440
00:13:07,376 --> 00:13:09,789
Hold on, hold on, hold on!

441
00:13:09,789 --> 00:13:10,644
Pull!!

442
00:13:10,644 --> 00:13:11,877
[Flop]
Pull, pull!

443
00:13:11,877 --> 00:13:14,471
[We're sorry, we cannot pull]
Pull! Pull, guys!

444
00:13:14,471 --> 00:13:16,134
Same there and here.

445
00:13:16,134 --> 00:13:17,810
[Dragging...]
No, DAWN! DAWN!

446
00:13:17,810 --> 00:13:19,267
Why aren't you pulling?

447
00:13:19,267 --> 00:13:21,260
DAWN! What are you doing leaning on me?!

448
00:13:21,260 --> 00:13:22,510
He was leaning on me!

449
00:13:22,510 --> 00:13:24,977
- No… I said I can't…
- Why were you leaning on me…

450
00:13:24,977 --> 00:13:26,377
[The paper doll senior can relate]
Hey, it's so hard, huh?

451
00:13:26,377 --> 00:13:27,410
- I'm going crazy.
- Lee Teuk!

452
00:13:27,410 --> 00:13:28,977
I realized it today!

453
00:13:28,977 --> 00:13:30,844
The Pyramid really
is a wonder of the world!

454
00:13:30,844 --> 00:13:32,077
[Those heavy stones]
It's impossible to build.

455
00:13:32,077 --> 00:13:34,477
[No way humans moved it]
There's no way they moved such huge stones.

456
00:13:34,477 --> 00:13:36,659
[Round 3: Shin Dong VS Johnny]
This is Round 3 of "Unwavering Trust".

457
00:13:36,659 --> 00:13:37,810
- I'll go first!
- Okay.

458
00:13:37,810 --> 00:13:39,391
Their turn could
be over as soon as it begins.

459
00:13:39,391 --> 00:13:41,831
- Then you can start.
- What?

460
00:13:41,831 --> 00:13:43,189
- Trust us!
- Okay.

461
00:13:43,189 --> 00:13:44,876
I'll finish it in one go!

462
00:13:44,876 --> 00:13:45,677
Phew...

463
00:13:45,677 --> 00:13:46,477
- Let's go?
- Ready.

464
00:13:46,477 --> 00:13:48,510
[Tense]
Yes, you can start!

465
00:13:48,510 --> 00:13:50,573
Let it go a little bit.

466
00:13:50,573 --> 00:13:51,776
Let it go a bit more.

467
00:13:51,776 --> 00:13:53,677
Now hold! Just slightly hold on.

468
00:13:53,677 --> 00:13:56,483
[Their lower bodies are leaning way back]
The moment it becomes like this…

469
00:13:56,483 --> 00:13:57,773
[Meanwhile, Shin Dong's sweeping the sand away]
Wait, what is he doing?

470
00:13:57,773 --> 00:13:59,496
Oh, so this is actually possible.

471
00:13:59,496 --> 00:14:00,959
- Is that right?
- Wait! You can only do it once!

472
00:14:00,959 --> 00:14:01,885
[Everyone's startled by the new technique]
How many times are you doing it?

473
00:14:01,885 --> 00:14:03,736
[Just pure torture]

474
00:14:03,736 --> 00:14:05,061
Pull me up!!!

475
00:14:05,061 --> 00:14:06,456
- Pull me up! We got it!
- AGHHHHH!

476
00:14:06,456 --> 00:14:08,577
[Shin Dong's tactic was to save his teammates' stamina]
Hey, come on! That's cheating!

477
00:14:08,577 --> 00:14:10,876
- You have to do it a lot in one turn!
- Is this allowed? Is it?

478
00:14:10,876 --> 00:14:12,676
Where'd that rule come from?

479
00:14:12,676 --> 00:14:13,877
[It's allowed in Ilsan]
From Ilsan. Ilsan.

480
00:14:13,877 --> 00:14:16,447
[Come on, Chicago guy]
Let's see how it's done in Chicago.

481
00:14:16,909 --> 00:14:17,977
[Chicago Guy has an overwhelming reach]

482
00:14:17,977 --> 00:14:20,252
Slowly, slowly!

483
00:14:20,252 --> 00:14:21,670
[Wobbling]
Okay!

484
00:14:21,670 --> 00:14:24,977
Something's off. It looks like
he's propping himself with his fingers.

485
00:14:24,977 --> 00:14:27,340
Up!

486
00:14:29,589 --> 00:14:31,410
[After struggling to lift him up,]
Up!

487
00:14:31,410 --> 00:14:33,310
[everyone exits together]

488
00:14:33,310 --> 00:14:34,897
My hands feel like
they're about to fall off.

489
00:14:34,897 --> 00:14:36,677
[It's all about who can hang on longer]
My hand's about to rip apart.

490
00:14:36,677 --> 00:14:38,043
Phew…

491
00:14:38,443 --> 00:14:39,543
[Lol]

492
00:14:39,543 --> 00:14:41,210
Shin Dong, you're not nervous, right?

493
00:14:41,210 --> 00:14:42,310
- Me?
- Yeah.

494
00:14:42,310 --> 00:14:44,076
They're the ones who are nervous.

495
00:14:44,076 --> 00:14:46,877
- Go?
- We were super nervous.

496
00:14:46,877 --> 00:14:48,365
[The faster they do it, the faster the pain ends]
Lower it, just a little bit.

497
00:14:48,365 --> 00:14:50,077
Lower it, lower it.

498
00:14:50,077 --> 00:14:51,710
Hold on!

499
00:14:51,710 --> 00:14:53,377
Pull up! Puuull uppp!

500
00:14:53,377 --> 00:14:54,244
That's it!

501
00:14:54,244 --> 00:14:55,444
- You gotta go, you gotta go.
- Here I go.

502
00:14:55,444 --> 00:14:56,934
Whoaaaa!!

503
00:14:56,934 --> 00:14:57,606
You gotta go.

504
00:14:57,606 --> 00:14:58,966
[Stretch]
Here I go.

505
00:14:59,744 --> 00:15:01,443
[Tremble, tremble]
Hey, watch your eyes!

506
00:15:01,443 --> 00:15:02,544
[A cheeky sand-splitting move]

507
00:15:02,544 --> 00:15:04,110
Oh! So cheeky!

508
00:15:06,509 --> 00:15:07,817
Ha!

509
00:15:07,817 --> 00:15:08,890
[100% serious]
Oh, stop!!

510
00:15:08,890 --> 00:15:10,677
[This isn't fun anymore...]
We can't do this now.

511
00:15:10,677 --> 00:15:12,137
My whole body hurts doing this.

512
00:15:12,137 --> 00:15:13,269
[Having the best time]
Let's go! We gotta hurry.

513
00:15:13,269 --> 00:15:15,037
- Let's go, let's go!
- We gotta hurry.

514
00:15:15,037 --> 00:15:16,277
- We gotta go!
- Lower, lower.

515
00:15:16,277 --> 00:15:17,177
- Gotta go! Just a little more!
- Lower, lower!

516
00:15:17,177 --> 00:15:18,929
Hold it… Hold it…!

517
00:15:18,929 --> 00:15:19,854
Ack…!

518
00:15:19,854 --> 00:15:21,245
- Hold it!
- No!

519
00:15:21,245 --> 00:15:22,144
[Danger]
Oh!

520
00:15:22,144 --> 00:15:24,376
[So fun]
He's kind of leaning forward!

521
00:15:24,376 --> 00:15:26,177
[Careful]
It's gonna fall, it's gonna fall!

522
00:15:26,177 --> 00:15:26,877
Shin Dong, hurry…

523
00:15:26,877 --> 00:15:28,177
- HURRY!!!!
- Oh, wait!

524
00:15:28,177 --> 00:15:29,177
- Pull up! Pull up!
- Hurry!

525
00:15:29,177 --> 00:15:29,977
Pull up!
It's good!

526
00:15:29,977 --> 00:15:31,876
[Plop]
Oh…

527
00:15:32,375 --> 00:15:34,493
[3 wins in a row]
[R3: Team Johnny wins]

528
00:15:34,493 --> 00:15:35,484
Yeah!!!

529
00:15:37,643 --> 00:15:40,150
[Legs give out]
Pick one, pick one!

530
00:15:40,150 --> 00:15:42,643
Your hands feel like
they're gonna fall off, huh?

531
00:15:42,643 --> 00:15:44,976
But I still lost 20kg.

532
00:15:44,976 --> 00:15:47,576
If it were my usual weight,
you would've all died!

533
00:15:47,576 --> 00:15:50,277
Since the first half's over,

534
00:15:50,277 --> 00:15:52,777
we're gonna tweak the rules
a bit to spice things up.

535
00:15:52,777 --> 00:15:53,977
Ooh! A rule change is good.

536
00:15:53,977 --> 00:15:56,677
[Go down at the same time]
You'll simultaneously go down and not come back up.

537
00:15:56,677 --> 00:15:58,177
Oh, okay.
Nice.

538
00:15:58,177 --> 00:16:00,377
- Take turns sweeping while staying in position?
- Yes.

539
00:16:00,377 --> 00:16:01,644
Okay, nice, nice.

540
00:16:01,644 --> 00:16:02,577
[It's all about endurance]
We've got a shot at this.

541
00:16:02,577 --> 00:16:03,877
- Yeah, that'd be pretty okay.
- Yeah.

542
00:16:03,877 --> 00:16:06,977
[Round 4: DAWN VS Lee Teuk]
"Unwavering Trust"! Ready!

543
00:16:06,977 --> 00:16:07,977
Slowly.

544
00:16:07,977 --> 00:16:09,877
[The two come down at the same time]
Slowly, slowly.

545
00:16:09,877 --> 00:16:11,298
- Let's hold it right here.
- Uh, wait, wait.

546
00:16:11,298 --> 00:16:12,766
- First, go down.
- Let's stay here.

547
00:16:12,766 --> 00:16:13,682
This is good.

548
00:16:13,682 --> 00:16:15,443
Press him down from above, DAWN!

549
00:16:15,443 --> 00:16:17,576
I'm good. Up…!
Oh, right, there's no "up"…

550
00:16:18,209 --> 00:16:21,443
[Have to keep swiping sand
while hanging on]

551
00:16:21,909 --> 00:16:24,876
[Basically, a battle of stamina]
Go up about this much… That's it.

552
00:16:25,843 --> 00:16:27,676
- Are you tired?
- A little…

553
00:16:27,676 --> 00:16:28,910
I'm so comfortable.

554
00:16:28,910 --> 00:16:31,476
[Unwavering comfort]
DAWN looks so relaxed.

555
00:16:31,476 --> 00:16:33,477
- Comfort… comfortable?!
- Hang in there.

556
00:16:33,477 --> 00:16:35,276
[This team is dying]

557
00:16:35,909 --> 00:16:37,673
That team's totally about to die.

558
00:16:37,673 --> 00:16:38,744
Are you really tired?

559
00:16:38,744 --> 00:16:41,251
- It's okayyyy…!
- Not even a little tired!

560
00:16:41,251 --> 00:16:42,977
- Mom!
- Come on!

561
00:16:42,977 --> 00:16:45,787
- DAWN, slow down. Let the other team tire out.
- Okay, Shin Dong.

562
00:16:45,787 --> 00:16:46,909
Hrrrgh...!

563
00:16:46,909 --> 00:16:48,743
Haah... Haah...

564
00:16:49,276 --> 00:16:51,521
[Their breathing gets heavier]

565
00:16:51,521 --> 00:16:53,576
[Worried]
I'll lift my back a bit...

566
00:16:53,576 --> 00:16:56,044
[I need to finish this quickly…!]

567
00:16:56,044 --> 00:16:57,316
[Drop]
Ack!

568
00:16:57,316 --> 00:16:59,284
[R4: Team Shin Dong's first win]
We lost, we lost.

569
00:16:59,284 --> 00:17:00,944
- Finally!
- Wow!

570
00:17:00,944 --> 00:17:04,809
[Cheering like they're princes]
Finally, finally!

571
00:17:04,809 --> 00:17:06,676
[Exhausted]

572
00:17:06,676 --> 00:17:08,442
- You okay?
- Fine.

573
00:17:08,902 --> 00:17:10,639
[My hand...]
Finally!

574
00:17:10,639 --> 00:17:12,608
[Choosing ramyun for the first time]
Hey, let's pick one with broth, like Shin Ramyun.

575
00:17:12,608 --> 00:17:14,060
I think I'll go with Buldak Ramen.

576
00:17:14,060 --> 00:17:14,977
[An extremely serious discussion]
Oh, me too.

577
00:17:14,977 --> 00:17:16,504
Since there's only one Buldak left,
let's go with Buldak.

578
00:17:16,504 --> 00:17:18,796
- Yeah, let's grab that one Buldak.
- Right, right.

579
00:17:19,249 --> 00:17:21,077
Wow! Nice!

580
00:17:21,077 --> 00:17:23,377
- Is your hand okay?
- Oh, it feels refreshing.

581
00:17:23,377 --> 00:17:25,303
This must really be difficult.

582
00:17:25,877 --> 00:17:27,577
[An urgent meeting after their first loss]
Should Lee Teuk and I handle this?

583
00:17:27,577 --> 00:17:29,284
Right? That'd be better?

584
00:17:29,284 --> 00:17:32,056
- Oh, there's a new strategy!
- A different strategy!

585
00:17:32,056 --> 00:17:33,483
There's a new strategy!

586
00:17:33,483 --> 00:17:35,176
[Isn't his butt]
Try going down once. Try it.

587
00:17:35,176 --> 00:17:36,588
[too in your face?]
Go down, go down.

588
00:17:36,588 --> 00:17:37,843
- Is this good?
- Yeah, go down.

589
00:17:37,843 --> 00:17:40,277
[A method for Stiff Ji Sung]

590
00:17:40,277 --> 00:17:41,805
[Slip]
But, wait, wait. He's slipping.

591
00:17:41,805 --> 00:17:43,473
[Since he's slipping, then…]
He's slipping, so… Oh, then let's move back.

592
00:17:43,473 --> 00:17:44,741
No, you have to hold him
from the back and grab him.

593
00:17:44,741 --> 00:17:46,178
[Changing into a strange position]
Then… Let's try it.

594
00:17:46,178 --> 00:17:47,042
That's way better.

595
00:17:47,042 --> 00:17:49,317
- I don't think Lee Teuk can hold him.
- I'll try it, I'll try.

596
00:17:50,780 --> 00:17:51,843
How's this?

597
00:17:51,843 --> 00:17:53,376
- Much better.
- Okay.

598
00:17:53,376 --> 00:17:54,644
Everyone, are you feeling tired?

599
00:17:54,644 --> 00:17:57,059
Just a little worn out.

600
00:17:57,059 --> 00:17:58,336
[Round 5: DAWN VS Ji Sung]
I'll go first.

601
00:17:58,336 --> 00:17:59,576
We'll go first.

602
00:17:59,576 --> 00:18:01,043
We'll begin the operation!

603
00:18:01,043 --> 00:18:02,476
[Teasing again]

604
00:18:02,476 --> 00:18:04,176
Alright, go. Keep on going.

605
00:18:04,176 --> 00:18:06,176
[Cheeky flapping]
Please go down, Ji Sung.

606
00:18:08,049 --> 00:18:09,177
Come on down.

607
00:18:09,177 --> 00:18:10,109
- That's it.
- Hold it.

608
00:18:10,109 --> 00:18:12,156
- How's it going, Ji Sung?
- Now, first…!

609
00:18:12,156 --> 00:18:12,910
You good, Ji Sung?

610
00:18:12,910 --> 00:18:14,304
- Yeah, yeah!
- A little higher, a little higher.

611
00:18:14,304 --> 00:18:15,976
- Nice, nice!
- Oh.

612
00:18:15,976 --> 00:18:17,044
- Pull up a little bit.
- Hold on!

613
00:18:17,044 --> 00:18:18,764
[Power teasing]
Let me add some spices.

614
00:18:18,764 --> 00:18:19,984
[This side's energy is fading fast]
Be bold. It's fine.

615
00:18:19,984 --> 00:18:21,789
[being in a terrible position]
The wind's not blowing.

616
00:18:21,789 --> 00:18:22,677
Pull up a bit.

617
00:18:22,677 --> 00:18:24,043
Hurry up while the wind's calm.

618
00:18:25,363 --> 00:18:26,568
Ha…!

619
00:18:28,177 --> 00:18:30,846
But like, everyone's
kind of losing their smiles.

620
00:18:30,846 --> 00:18:34,002
My forearms feel like
they're gonna explode!

621
00:18:34,409 --> 00:18:35,577
- Ha...
- This is the crucial part.

622
00:18:35,577 --> 00:18:37,074
- Ha…!
- Almost there, almost there.

623
00:18:37,074 --> 00:18:38,676
[Their energy is fading along with the sand]
Go easy, go easy!

624
00:18:41,611 --> 00:18:43,209
Oh, I'll quickly go down!

625
00:18:43,976 --> 00:18:45,776
[The flag fell!]
Oh!

626
00:18:45,776 --> 00:18:46,876
- Ugh!
- Oh!

627
00:18:46,876 --> 00:18:47,879
[Whoosh]
Oh, we won.

628
00:18:47,879 --> 00:18:48,685
Did we lose? Did we lose?

629
00:18:48,685 --> 00:18:51,071
- The wind, the wind!
- Agh!!

630
00:18:51,071 --> 00:18:52,576
[Everyone's utterly wiped out]
The wind's really strong.

631
00:18:52,576 --> 00:18:54,811
- Good job, Ji Sung. Good job.
- You all did great too.

632
00:18:54,811 --> 00:18:56,580
Why does it feel
like we're the winners?

633
00:18:56,580 --> 00:18:58,210
Seriously, why does it feel like we won?

634
00:18:58,210 --> 00:19:00,177
[The totally exhausted winners]
I don't think they'll be able to eat ramyun.

635
00:19:00,177 --> 00:19:02,381
I don't think they'll have
the energy to hold up their chopsticks.

636
00:19:02,381 --> 00:19:03,425
[Mid-game check-in]
Okay, right now the total is

637
00:19:03,425 --> 00:19:04,187
4.

638
00:19:04,187 --> 00:19:05,543
1.

639
00:19:05,543 --> 00:19:06,577
Should we do one more round?

640
00:19:06,577 --> 00:19:08,277
[Johnny VS Shin Dong]
Then Johnny and I will do it

641
00:19:08,277 --> 00:19:09,298
[Endurance?]
as a game of endurance.

642
00:19:09,298 --> 00:19:11,292
[Oh, this sounds fun]
I think it'll come out this time around.

643
00:19:11,292 --> 00:19:12,498
Everyone's tired.

644
00:19:12,498 --> 00:19:14,369
Will we be able to hold on…?

645
00:19:14,369 --> 00:19:15,810
[Might die before eating ramyun...]
Right now, there's Shin Ramyun and Yukgaejang.

646
00:19:15,810 --> 00:19:17,873
This is actually
a bigger problem for me.

647
00:19:17,873 --> 00:19:19,876
[Painful groans are heard from everywhere]
Wow, but I'm already so tired.

648
00:19:19,876 --> 00:19:22,162
- Will we be able to hang on?
- DAWN, you're nervous, huh?

649
00:19:22,162 --> 00:19:23,373
- Yeah.
- I'm nervous too.

650
00:19:23,373 --> 00:19:25,961
[Why is this so hard...]
This is seriously tough, right?

651
00:19:25,961 --> 00:19:28,844
[Let's just outlast the other team]
Let's just try to hold on longer than them.

652
00:19:28,844 --> 00:19:32,809
[Round 6: Shin Dong VS Johnny]
Here we go. It's the last round. Ready!

653
00:19:33,988 --> 00:19:36,444
[The two guys slowly lower themselves]
Let's go, let's go, go!

654
00:19:36,444 --> 00:19:38,469
- We have to go down, go down.
- Slowly!

655
00:19:43,258 --> 00:19:45,629
[Almost touching the ground]
I'll go first.

656
00:19:45,629 --> 00:19:47,547
- Okay.
- Sit down a little, sit down a little.

657
00:19:49,175 --> 00:19:50,477
Sit down a little.
Sit down a little.

658
00:19:50,477 --> 00:19:51,675
We're good now.

659
00:19:51,675 --> 00:19:54,077
Hey, what's this?!
What's happening here?

660
00:19:54,077 --> 00:19:55,777
[Suddenly rolling on the ground...]
What's happening here?

661
00:19:55,777 --> 00:19:57,410
- What are you doing?
- Ji Sung…!

662
00:19:57,410 --> 00:19:59,057
- Ji Sung, how can you just suddenly let go?
- What are you doing?

663
00:19:59,057 --> 00:20:00,877
Ji Sung...

664
00:20:00,877 --> 00:20:02,976
He suddenly let go!

665
00:20:02,976 --> 00:20:05,309
[Ji Sung was shaky from the start]
Sit down a little, sit down a little.

666
00:20:05,843 --> 00:20:06,892
[Tried to switch his foot position]
Sit down a little.

667
00:20:06,892 --> 00:20:08,177
[But lost his balance]
We're good now.

668
00:20:08,177 --> 00:20:09,909
Hey, what's this?!

669
00:20:09,909 --> 00:20:11,274
[The game ended anticlimactically]
My heel was off the ground,

670
00:20:11,274 --> 00:20:13,277
so I tried to support it,
but lost my balance.

671
00:20:13,277 --> 00:20:14,090
One more time...

672
00:20:14,090 --> 00:20:16,493
[Yeah, nope]
Just once, just once!

673
00:20:16,493 --> 00:20:17,627
It's okay, it's okay!

674
00:20:17,627 --> 00:20:19,377
From the start…!

675
00:20:19,377 --> 00:20:21,343
You were nervous, huh?

676
00:20:21,769 --> 00:20:22,976
So funny!

677
00:20:22,976 --> 00:20:23,976
Ji Sung!

678
00:20:23,976 --> 00:20:25,577
Did you suddenly
not wanna play anymore?

679
00:20:25,577 --> 00:20:28,276
[Feeling wronged]
I really tried my best!

680
00:20:31,081 --> 00:20:33,089
And with that,
the official round has ended.

681
00:20:33,089 --> 00:20:33,976
Yes.

682
00:20:33,976 --> 00:20:35,577
To eat the ramyun, everyone…

683
00:20:35,577 --> 00:20:36,944
- No way?!
- You need water.

684
00:20:36,944 --> 00:20:38,765
- Are we really playing again for water?
- No way!

685
00:20:38,765 --> 00:20:41,049
- With Kimchi on the line.
- Yes! We need Kimchi.

686
00:20:41,049 --> 00:20:41,985
[Winner takes all]
Only one round.

687
00:20:41,985 --> 00:20:43,079
- One round. Okay!
- One round.

688
00:20:43,079 --> 00:20:44,688
[Game: Hang & Steal the Hat]
It's "Steal the Hat".

689
00:20:44,688 --> 00:20:46,567
- While hanging like this?
- Yes.

690
00:20:46,567 --> 00:20:48,844
Oh, but I'm too tired
to do this now…

691
00:20:48,844 --> 00:20:50,393
- You have to do it.
- I have to do it?

692
00:20:50,393 --> 00:20:51,477
We'll hold him up.

693
00:20:51,477 --> 00:20:52,948
[This team's so confident]
We're totally gonna win.

694
00:20:52,948 --> 00:20:54,761
We have to do it.
We'll win it.

695
00:20:54,761 --> 00:20:56,976
- Let's do this.
- Let's at least bring some Kimchi.

696
00:20:56,976 --> 00:20:58,477
[Team Shin Dong: Yo Han]
It's good, right?

697
00:20:58,477 --> 00:20:59,369
It's good!

698
00:20:59,369 --> 00:21:02,209
[Team Johnny: Lee Teuk]
I feel like they'll be quick.

699
00:21:02,209 --> 00:21:04,187
[Talking trash]
He knows how to use his body,

700
00:21:04,187 --> 00:21:06,023
- but he's kind of bad at things like this.
- I know, right?

701
00:21:06,023 --> 00:21:07,480
Yo Han's good at using his feet,

702
00:21:07,480 --> 00:21:09,485
but not his hands.

703
00:21:09,485 --> 00:21:11,580
- Pretend you didn't hear that.
- Should we do a quick preview?

704
00:21:11,580 --> 00:21:13,077
- A quick preview?
- To see the distance.

705
00:21:13,077 --> 00:21:14,873
[A distance check before the main game]
Alright, here we go. Keep going!

706
00:21:14,873 --> 00:21:16,139
Keep going!

707
00:21:16,139 --> 00:21:17,680
Lee Teuk, come a bit more.

708
00:21:17,680 --> 00:21:18,609
[Burst]

709
00:21:20,377 --> 00:21:21,777
This is fun!
This is fun! This is fun!

710
00:21:21,777 --> 00:21:24,775
[Why are they suddenly laughing?]
This is fun! This is fun! This is fun!

711
00:21:24,775 --> 00:21:26,795
[That was so childish just now]
We're so childish.

712
00:21:26,795 --> 00:21:29,035
- So childish.
- Alright, let's get started.

713
00:21:29,035 --> 00:21:31,190
[A one-round showdown for Kimchi: Yo Han vs Lee Teuk]
One round with Kimchi on the line!

714
00:21:31,190 --> 00:21:32,220
Ready!

715
00:21:33,169 --> 00:21:35,067
[The two slowly inch closer]
Oh, it's happening.

716
00:21:35,067 --> 00:21:36,168
No, I gotta go up!

717
00:21:36,168 --> 00:21:37,310
[Uhehehehehe]

718
00:21:37,310 --> 00:21:38,177
I gotta go up!

719
00:21:38,177 --> 00:21:40,269
I can't go any lower than this!

720
00:21:40,269 --> 00:21:41,384
[Right from the start,]
I gotta move up more!

721
00:21:41,384 --> 00:21:42,564
[Yo Han starts attacking]
I can't go lower!

722
00:21:42,564 --> 00:21:43,865
I really can't go any lower!

723
00:21:43,865 --> 00:21:44,777
Lee Teuk, we're going!

724
00:21:44,777 --> 00:21:47,969
[Johnny loosens the rope just a bit]
Lee Teuk, here we go! Go! Go!

725
00:21:47,969 --> 00:21:49,209
[Here I come…!]

726
00:21:50,356 --> 00:21:52,676
[Almost lost his hat
while trying to steal Yo Han's...!]

727
00:21:52,676 --> 00:21:55,043
[Timing coordination is everything]
But you're way too fast! Too fast!

728
00:21:55,043 --> 00:21:56,444
Right now!!!

729
00:21:56,444 --> 00:21:58,275
[Roar]

730
00:21:58,275 --> 00:21:59,576
A little slower, slower.

731
00:22:04,476 --> 00:22:06,876
[But why is it slowly getting…]

732
00:22:06,876 --> 00:22:08,544
[Giggle, giggle]

733
00:22:08,544 --> 00:22:09,977
Hey, hurry up already!!!!!

734
00:22:09,977 --> 00:22:13,977
Why are these two so happy…

735
00:22:13,977 --> 00:22:15,987
- Why are they so happy?
- Wait, wait!

736
00:22:15,987 --> 00:22:18,509
[What's their deal????]
When are you gonna do it?

737
00:22:18,509 --> 00:22:21,183
[These two are just dying from laughing]
Oh, wait…!

738
00:22:21,183 --> 00:22:22,770
Why are you so happy?

739
00:22:22,770 --> 00:22:24,577
Sorry, but it's only
funny for you two!

740
00:22:24,577 --> 00:22:26,277
It's not fun for us!!

741
00:22:26,277 --> 00:22:27,977
Oh, my stomach!

742
00:22:27,977 --> 00:22:29,210
Wanna give it a try?

743
00:22:29,210 --> 00:22:30,269
It's seriously hilarious!

744
00:22:30,269 --> 00:22:31,877
Seriously hilarious!

745
00:22:31,877 --> 00:22:33,377
["Steal the Hat" recommended for]
If people who don't get along

746
00:22:33,377 --> 00:22:35,044
or are in a fight do this,

747
00:22:35,044 --> 00:22:36,577
they'll end up falling in love.

748
00:22:36,577 --> 00:22:38,929
It's not fun for us!

749
00:22:38,929 --> 00:22:41,579
[Calm down and restart the game]
Let's go! Please blow the whistle!

750
00:22:41,579 --> 00:22:42,776
Ow, my ribs hurt.

751
00:22:42,776 --> 00:22:44,080
Get ready!
[Go]

752
00:22:44,080 --> 00:22:44,996
- Let go! Let go!
- Slowly!

753
00:22:44,996 --> 00:22:46,002
Go!

754
00:22:46,002 --> 00:22:48,070
[Danger]
Go down more! That's it.

755
00:22:48,070 --> 00:22:49,081
- Pfft…!
- Let's go down a little more.

756
00:22:49,081 --> 00:22:51,277
- Hey, your hat!
- You went even lower!

757
00:22:51,277 --> 00:22:52,177
- Ha ha ha ha ha ha!
- Ha ha ha ha ha ha!

758
00:22:52,177 --> 00:22:54,227
Now's the time, now's the time!

759
00:22:54,977 --> 00:22:56,977
[Seriously, what's wrong with you two?]
Why though?!

760
00:22:56,977 --> 00:22:58,685
They just start laughing
whenever they make eye contact.

761
00:22:58,685 --> 00:23:00,581
It hurts!

762
00:23:02,944 --> 00:23:05,386
[Their laughter somehow
spreads to everyone]

763
00:23:05,386 --> 00:23:07,466
- I'm actually about to cry!
- Try this, just try it!

764
00:23:07,466 --> 00:23:08,774
[Highly recommended]
Can you please just try it once?

765
00:23:08,774 --> 00:23:09,935
- Just try it once…
- It feels strange.

766
00:23:09,935 --> 00:23:11,270
It feels weird!

767
00:23:11,270 --> 00:23:13,277
- This… feels weird!
- Switch players?

768
00:23:13,277 --> 00:23:14,804
- Just try it once, for real!
- Switch players, switch players.

769
00:23:14,804 --> 00:23:15,894
[A precious experience he really wants to share]
DAWN, just try it once.

770
00:23:15,894 --> 00:23:17,165
Switch to DAWN.

771
00:23:17,165 --> 00:23:18,477
Take off your sunglasses!

772
00:23:18,477 --> 00:23:20,569
Look each other in the eyes.

773
00:23:20,569 --> 00:23:21,583
Right?

774
00:23:21,583 --> 00:23:22,385
[The feeling lingers]
Just once…!

775
00:23:22,385 --> 00:23:23,412
It's seriously so hilarious.

776
00:23:23,412 --> 00:23:25,076
It hurts so much here.

777
00:23:25,076 --> 00:23:26,661
Hehehehe...

778
00:23:26,661 --> 00:23:28,510
He's still laughing. Oh, it hurts.

779
00:23:28,510 --> 00:23:30,477
I think it'll come out in my dreams.

780
00:23:30,477 --> 00:23:33,789
[Lee Teuk's face that he saw up close]
His expressions when we got close.

781
00:23:33,789 --> 00:23:34,895
[Player switch due to unstoppable laughing]
Let's try it out.

782
00:23:34,895 --> 00:23:36,558
- Hey, Johnny, try going down.
- I'll give it a try.

783
00:23:36,558 --> 00:23:38,060
Go down.

784
00:23:38,060 --> 00:23:39,969
- Go down, go down.
- I'll hold you.

785
00:23:42,243 --> 00:23:45,802
[They're unable to hold back their laughter]

786
00:23:45,802 --> 00:23:47,203
[See, I told you!]
I told you, right?

787
00:23:47,203 --> 00:23:48,577
I'm telling you, it's true!

788
00:23:48,577 --> 00:23:51,110
[What kind of spell am I under?]
This makes a person look like this!

789
00:23:51,110 --> 00:23:54,109
No, seriously,
you only see from here, like this.

790
00:23:54,109 --> 00:23:55,590
[If you want to be in love,
play "Steal the Hat"…]

791
00:23:55,590 --> 00:23:56,864
I'm telling you, this is hilarious!

792
00:23:56,864 --> 00:23:58,276
Oh, Johnny!

793
00:23:58,276 --> 00:24:00,943
This was actually a really fun game.

794
00:24:00,943 --> 00:24:02,277
[With Kimchi really on the line]
Johnny's really athletic.

795
00:24:02,277 --> 00:24:03,479
[Shin Dong VS Johnny]
Get ready!

796
00:24:04,270 --> 00:24:08,375
[You can't have ramyun without Kimchi]
Come on, Shin Dong's good at grabbing!

797
00:24:09,476 --> 00:24:11,561
[Slips]
Oh, we gotta adjust the position.

798
00:24:11,561 --> 00:24:13,216
We gotta adjust the position.

799
00:24:15,069 --> 00:24:16,877
[After a quick brush]

800
00:24:16,877 --> 00:24:18,877
[He goes right back for it]

801
00:24:18,877 --> 00:24:20,109
[Trying again]

802
00:24:20,777 --> 00:24:22,909
[Shin Dong pushes hard from the start]

803
00:24:27,809 --> 00:24:33,250
[Let's check what happened
from a different angle]

804
00:24:33,250 --> 00:24:35,676
[Behind the fierce duel]

805
00:24:35,676 --> 00:24:37,609
[The supporters wobble]

806
00:24:39,129 --> 00:24:42,876
[This is as far as we go, Captain…]

807
00:24:47,037 --> 00:24:48,944
[We fought with no regrets...]
They're unable to hold on over there.

808
00:24:48,944 --> 00:24:50,710
They're unable to hold on.

809
00:24:50,710 --> 00:24:51,683
[Team Shin Dong wins the Kimchi!]
Kimchi!

810
00:24:51,683 --> 00:24:53,976
- Kimchi!
- Kimchi!

811
00:24:54,404 --> 00:24:57,076
But why is this game
the most fun so far?

812
00:24:57,076 --> 00:24:59,676
This isn't even
an "ALL or NOTHING" game.

813
00:25:00,493 --> 00:25:01,777
[What even is this…]
I think Cola would be

814
00:25:01,777 --> 00:25:03,075
[Using up all their energy laughing]
more popular in a hot country.

815
00:25:03,075 --> 00:25:04,368
- Definitely.
- Yeah.

816
00:25:05,382 --> 00:25:09,443
[A rare lunch with everyone]

817
00:25:10,809 --> 00:25:13,709
(Quickly recovered his energy)

818
00:25:14,176 --> 00:25:15,177
Wow!

819
00:25:15,177 --> 00:25:16,843
Amazing!

820
00:25:17,776 --> 00:25:21,276
[All prepared for WANGGEOZ,
who worked very hard]

821
00:25:22,109 --> 00:25:24,076
[Pick and eat whatever you'd like]

822
00:25:24,476 --> 00:25:27,143
[Starting with rice / bread / noodles]

823
00:25:28,909 --> 00:25:31,276
[A spread of meat and seafood]

824
00:25:32,276 --> 00:25:35,876
[A perfect meal,
even with sweet and tangy desserts]

825
00:25:38,176 --> 00:25:41,243
[Please enjoy]

826
00:25:41,976 --> 00:25:44,643
(Taking a bite of the risotto first)

827
00:25:45,176 --> 00:25:46,709
Mmm!

828
00:25:48,676 --> 00:25:49,344
[Amazing]
Mmm!

829
00:25:49,344 --> 00:25:51,343
[Eating nonstop]

830
00:25:52,143 --> 00:25:54,083
(Should I bite into it...)

831
00:25:54,083 --> 00:25:56,049
(Let's just eat it all in one bite)

832
00:25:57,076 --> 00:25:58,477
Egypt really knows
how to make a good burger.

833
00:25:58,477 --> 00:26:00,809
[Both cheeks stuffed full]

834
00:26:01,676 --> 00:26:04,109
[It's a burger hotspot?]
I gotta try the burger.

835
00:26:04,676 --> 00:26:06,909
[Jumping on the burger trend]

836
00:26:08,076 --> 00:26:11,243
[The eldest's pick is cream pasta]

837
00:26:13,109 --> 00:26:16,643
[Yo Han follows Lee Teuk's lead
and takes a bite of pasta]

838
00:26:17,576 --> 00:26:20,609
(Taking a bite of the taco)

839
00:26:21,843 --> 00:26:24,060
Wow!

840
00:26:24,060 --> 00:26:25,286
- This is good.
- It's good?

841
00:26:25,286 --> 00:26:27,445
[Agreed]
Yeah, it's good.

842
00:26:27,445 --> 00:26:29,291
[If it's tasty, gotta try it]
Want some? Here, take it.

843
00:26:29,291 --> 00:26:31,573
I highly recommend it.

844
00:26:32,666 --> 00:26:36,476
[Everyone fills up with what they each like]
That's when you eat this quickly.

845
00:26:37,476 --> 00:26:40,709
[A short break before the next schedule]
Oh, I ate so well.

846
00:26:41,643 --> 00:26:43,513
Should we find
a spot to lie down?

847
00:26:43,513 --> 00:26:45,421
- Here?
- Is it here?

848
00:26:47,169 --> 00:26:48,978
- Oh, this is it.
- Wow, this place is so nice.

849
00:26:48,978 --> 00:26:51,009
[Lying down on sunbeds right by the sea]
This is it, this is it!

850
00:26:52,163 --> 00:26:53,570
The water's seriously so clear.

851
00:26:53,570 --> 00:26:55,543
How can it be this clear?

852
00:26:55,543 --> 00:26:58,343
[The refreshing Red Sea
spread out before your eyes]

853
00:26:58,776 --> 00:27:00,624
Something about this clean water

854
00:27:00,624 --> 00:27:02,776
makes me think there are
other edible fish living in it.

855
00:27:02,776 --> 00:27:04,366
Don't most people just call it "fish"?

856
00:27:04,366 --> 00:27:05,586
It's not "edible fish"?

857
00:27:05,586 --> 00:27:07,777
[Anyway]
So, wouldn't there be lots of tropical fish?

858
00:27:07,777 --> 00:27:09,377
But is the water warm?

859
00:27:09,377 --> 00:27:11,675
It's not warm.

860
00:27:11,675 --> 00:27:13,943
Don't tropical fish live in warm water..?

861
00:27:13,943 --> 00:27:15,668
If it's warm… wouldn't they get cooked?

862
00:27:15,668 --> 00:27:17,376
[What is this…?] But they're tropical fish (yeol-dae-eo).

863
00:27:17,376 --> 00:27:20,410
They're not tropical fish because
it has the word "heat (yeol)" in the name.

864
00:27:20,410 --> 00:27:22,709
Then? Are they tropical fish
because there are "10 (yeol)" of them?

865
00:27:22,709 --> 00:27:25,676
[Wow, this conversation is
on a whole different level]

866
00:27:25,676 --> 00:27:28,001
If people overheard us chatting...

867
00:27:28,001 --> 00:27:29,624
They'd think,
"Ugh, these ignorant fools…"

868
00:27:29,624 --> 00:27:30,659
Lee Teuk, please look it up.

869
00:27:30,659 --> 00:27:32,977
[Confident]
Tropical fish are the ones that live in warm water.

870
00:27:32,977 --> 00:27:34,477
(Searching...)

871
00:27:34,477 --> 00:27:36,476
- Oh! Shin Dong!
- Hmm?

872
00:27:36,476 --> 00:27:39,078
They usually live in warm water
around 20 to 30 degrees.

873
00:27:39,078 --> 00:27:40,544
[Fish that live in tropical or subtropical regions]
See? I told you I was right.

874
00:27:40,544 --> 00:27:44,491
Tropical fish… That's why
people who have big aquariums

875
00:27:44,491 --> 00:27:46,980
[Told you I was right]
have to constantly adjust the water temperature.

876
00:27:48,477 --> 00:27:50,977
But our conversation right now...

877
00:27:50,977 --> 00:27:53,515
[Is this even right...?]
Why are we even talking about this...?

878
00:27:53,515 --> 00:27:56,677
[The important thing isn't tropical fish]
Whether a fish's body temperature drops or rises

879
00:27:56,677 --> 00:27:58,296
isn't really important.

880
00:27:58,296 --> 00:27:59,677
[The tropical fish will be fine]
Whether we end up as princes

881
00:27:59,677 --> 00:28:00,810
or paupers is what's important…

882
00:28:00,810 --> 00:28:03,170
Ha Ha Ha Ha Ha Ha!

883
00:28:03,170 --> 00:28:05,794
You and I have been a prince
and a pauper the same amount of times.

884
00:28:05,794 --> 00:28:06,967
That's right.

885
00:28:06,967 --> 00:28:10,177
Sorry to the younger guys,
but if we put in a bit more effort,

886
00:28:10,177 --> 00:28:12,135
we can totally become princes.

887
00:28:12,135 --> 00:28:13,683
[Deciding to play dirty against the younger members]
If we play a little dirty…

888
00:28:13,683 --> 00:28:14,884
Play dirty?

889
00:28:14,884 --> 00:28:17,372
From what I saw,
they don't have much experience,

890
00:28:17,372 --> 00:28:19,374
so they're bad at strategizing.

891
00:28:19,374 --> 00:28:22,544
For a second, this crossed my mind.

892
00:28:22,544 --> 00:28:24,876
"Are we being... too soft?"

893
00:28:24,876 --> 00:28:26,877
[Just how much]
I think we need to try harder to win.

894
00:28:26,877 --> 00:28:28,583
I think we need to
really push ourselves.

895
00:28:28,583 --> 00:28:31,376
[do we have to…]
Hey wait, hold up, lift me up!

896
00:28:31,376 --> 00:28:33,743
[push ourselves…?]

897
00:28:34,392 --> 00:28:35,777
Lee Teuk, what do you think?
Should we team up?

898
00:28:35,777 --> 00:28:36,876
[I'm in!]
Let's team up.

899
00:28:36,876 --> 00:28:38,577
[The Soft Brothers in one team?]
Then should we have another round of Old Boy today?

900
00:28:38,577 --> 00:28:39,477
Let's push hard.

901
00:28:39,477 --> 00:28:43,444
And if the two of us stick together,
people might get suspicious,

902
00:28:43,444 --> 00:28:44,676
so should we recruit someone?

903
00:28:44,676 --> 00:28:46,244
I think DAWN would be perfect.

904
00:28:46,244 --> 00:28:47,277
(Agreed)

905
00:28:47,277 --> 00:28:48,277
I'm thinking DAWN is good.

906
00:28:48,277 --> 00:28:50,443
[Currently all princes]
[DAWN's energy is too strong to ignore]

907
00:28:50,872 --> 00:28:54,043
[Suddenly tired after all the planning]
Alright, I'm gonna nap a little bit.

908
00:28:54,909 --> 00:28:57,976
[And so, the older members chatted away
about tropical fish and playing dirty…]

909
00:28:59,409 --> 00:29:03,343
[And napped to the sound of crashing waves]

910
00:29:07,909 --> 00:29:10,543
(Who are these people…)

911
00:29:11,609 --> 00:29:14,943
[For some reason, it feels like
he's wandering through the underworld]

912
00:29:19,743 --> 00:29:22,177
What are you doing right now?

913
00:29:22,177 --> 00:29:25,076
I'm taking in all of Egypt.

914
00:29:25,476 --> 00:29:27,909
[DAWN, who totally
soaked up Egypt's energy,]

915
00:29:28,743 --> 00:29:32,009
[used that energy to work on music...]

916
00:29:33,143 --> 00:29:36,243
[And found some peace of mind...]

917
00:29:36,976 --> 00:29:39,809
[Clearly a travel YouTuber]

918
00:29:40,643 --> 00:29:42,676
Hey Johnny!

919
00:29:42,676 --> 00:29:45,677
[Found Johnny chilling]
What are you doing on this beautiful island?

920
00:29:45,677 --> 00:29:48,344
Johnny, I'll take your picture.
Can I take a picture of you?

921
00:29:48,344 --> 00:29:49,416
[Sounds good]
Sure.

922
00:29:49,809 --> 00:29:52,272
[Taking pictures of his little bro
with the film camera he brought himself]

923
00:29:52,272 --> 00:29:53,301
Wow!

924
00:29:53,301 --> 00:29:54,049
(Hot guy pose)

925
00:29:54,049 --> 00:29:55,581
That's insane…

926
00:29:56,104 --> 00:29:57,577
Do you take photos often?

927
00:29:57,577 --> 00:30:00,081
I usually don't take them outdoors.

928
00:30:00,081 --> 00:30:04,166
Mostly in studios.

929
00:30:04,948 --> 00:30:07,037
(Prefers studios)
I take lots of photos in the studio.

930
00:30:08,043 --> 00:30:09,818
I'll take photos for you later.

931
00:30:09,818 --> 00:30:11,340
That'd be nice…

932
00:30:11,340 --> 00:30:12,710
[Slightly touched]
Then I'd be thankful.

933
00:30:12,710 --> 00:30:14,444
How much can you pay me?

934
00:30:14,444 --> 00:30:15,477
[I never said it was free.]

935
00:30:15,477 --> 00:30:17,409
[Heh...]
How much can you pay me?

936
00:30:17,409 --> 00:30:19,209
(Thinking)

937
00:30:19,836 --> 00:30:22,558
DAWN, what's your rate?

938
00:30:22,558 --> 00:30:24,377
I charge minimum wage.

939
00:30:24,377 --> 00:30:26,576
[Deal]
Oh, then…!

940
00:30:26,576 --> 00:30:28,510
Then I'll shoot for 2 hours.

941
00:30:28,510 --> 00:30:30,248
(Cheap)
Alright, 22,000 won.

942
00:30:30,248 --> 00:30:31,874
Okay, okay.

943
00:30:31,874 --> 00:30:33,943
[This is the hot guy from Chicago]
The model definitely helps.

944
00:30:34,443 --> 00:30:36,476
[Maximum output for minimum wage]

945
00:30:36,909 --> 00:30:39,144
[The next model is Ji Sung]
Ji Sung, stand over there. Anywhere is fine.

946
00:30:39,144 --> 00:30:40,709
Nice!

947
00:30:40,709 --> 00:30:42,176
[Fixing his hair]

948
00:30:43,076 --> 00:30:45,443
[How do I look?]

949
00:30:46,076 --> 00:30:49,276
[After wrapping up a nice photo shoot…]
Nice!

950
00:30:49,889 --> 00:30:51,384
[He takes a nice stroll with Yo Han in the wind]
Wow.

951
00:30:51,384 --> 00:30:53,076
- Hmm.
- Wow, this wind is really…!

952
00:30:55,298 --> 00:30:59,910
We look like reporters covering a typhoon zone…

953
00:30:59,910 --> 00:31:01,210
[Ready to roll]

954
00:31:01,210 --> 00:31:03,110
We're reporting live on location!

955
00:31:03,110 --> 00:31:05,442
[Kim Yo Han / One-day reporter]

956
00:31:05,442 --> 00:31:08,209
[In awe]
Wow, but this place is just...!

957
00:31:08,849 --> 00:31:12,898
[The endless blue sea stretching beyond the wind]
This place is insane, seriously insane.

958
00:31:12,898 --> 00:31:14,307
This is pretty too, right?

959
00:31:16,467 --> 00:31:18,877
[But]
I was thinking...

960
00:31:18,877 --> 00:31:21,984
I thought,
"It might be okay to be a pauper today…"

961
00:31:21,984 --> 00:31:23,084
[Firm]
I don't think so.

962
00:31:23,084 --> 00:31:25,492
- No, hey!
- If we sleep outside today,

963
00:31:25,492 --> 00:31:27,876
when we wake up tomorrow,
we might be on a different island.

964
00:31:27,876 --> 00:31:29,688
[Paupers flying in the strong wind]
We'll get blown away and end up over there.

965
00:31:29,688 --> 00:31:32,169
I seriously think that might happen!

966
00:31:33,103 --> 00:31:36,085
[Quietly getting pummeled by the wind...]
Wow, but right now, it's really…

967
00:31:36,085 --> 00:31:37,375
(The sand is free of charge)
There's so much sand blowing over.

968
00:31:37,375 --> 00:31:39,493
My throat's burning.

969
00:31:40,789 --> 00:31:43,077
The real problem is...

970
00:31:43,077 --> 00:31:46,091
the wind's only
gonna get stronger at night...

971
00:31:46,091 --> 00:31:49,976
[Correct]
Wow, this place is no joke. What do we do?

972
00:31:50,866 --> 00:31:53,677
[To avoid the wind,
they move to a different spot]

973
00:31:53,677 --> 00:31:56,243
[Curious]
Hey, what happens if you press this doll?

974
00:31:56,243 --> 00:31:57,976
[Wanna hear?]
Just…

975
00:32:00,576 --> 00:32:01,710
[Oh…]

976
00:32:01,710 --> 00:32:03,609
[Shouldn't have asked]

977
00:32:04,276 --> 00:32:06,709
[Proud owner]
[My baby sings well, right?]

978
00:32:07,343 --> 00:32:10,457
Out of all the games so far,
which one was the most fun?

979
00:32:10,457 --> 00:32:11,744
The quizzes for me!

980
00:32:11,744 --> 00:32:12,653
[At Luxor Temple]
"The Sphinx's Riddle"!

981
00:32:12,653 --> 00:32:14,792
Yeah, solving quizzes
was the most fun.

982
00:32:14,792 --> 00:32:17,750
[Thinking back]
Why was I…

983
00:32:17,750 --> 00:32:19,765
so motivated to solve the quizzes?

984
00:32:19,765 --> 00:32:21,365
Why did I try so hard?

985
00:32:21,365 --> 00:32:23,259
Because we saw hope...

986
00:32:23,259 --> 00:32:25,742
[Deep realization!]
Oh! It's because we saw hope!

987
00:32:25,742 --> 00:32:27,045
Even for "Speaking in 9 languages,"
we lost by one language.

988
00:32:27,045 --> 00:32:28,977
- That's right, that's right!
- Because we saw hope…

989
00:32:28,977 --> 00:32:30,072
[Sometimes, hope brings even greater despair]

990
00:32:30,072 --> 00:32:32,195
Ji Sung went crazy.

991
00:32:32,195 --> 00:32:34,464
[Victory is just ahead]
[They racked their brains as hard as they could]

992
00:32:34,464 --> 00:32:35,677
Round 1 goes to Team OB!

993
00:32:35,677 --> 00:32:38,209
[Lost a round with the older members
a step ahead of them]

994
00:32:39,776 --> 00:32:40,869
[Next round flows without a hitch]

995
00:32:40,869 --> 00:32:42,737
- Poppin'!
- Correct!

996
00:32:42,737 --> 00:32:43,569
Correct!

997
00:32:43,569 --> 00:32:45,479
[Hehe! Looks like
we'll really become princes…!!!!!!]

998
00:32:45,479 --> 00:32:47,471
He knows the most about DAWN!

999
00:32:47,471 --> 00:32:50,509
[Not a chance]
I'm the prince!

1000
00:32:51,544 --> 00:32:53,510
[Harbored way too much hope]

1001
00:32:53,510 --> 00:32:54,877
[Hnng]

1002
00:32:54,877 --> 00:32:56,976
- Wow…
- My legs hurt.

1003
00:32:56,976 --> 00:32:59,155
He threw water bottles…

1004
00:32:59,155 --> 00:33:01,344
[It was like that back then…]
He slid…

1005
00:33:01,344 --> 00:33:03,669
[Their break ends with reminiscing]
I don't remember the day I threw the water bottle.

1006
00:33:03,669 --> 00:33:05,860
But I think I did.

1007
00:33:05,860 --> 00:33:06,732
Let's go.

1008
00:33:06,732 --> 00:33:09,010
[WANGGEOZ reunite]
Let's go, let's go.

1009
00:33:09,010 --> 00:33:10,877
- Did you enjoy your meal?
- Yes!

1010
00:33:10,877 --> 00:33:11,877
When are you having ramyun?

1011
00:33:11,877 --> 00:33:13,084
[Saving ramyun for a late-night snack]
At night.

1012
00:33:13,084 --> 00:33:14,877
- At night.
- That's right. We'll eat ramyun at night.

1013
00:33:14,877 --> 00:33:17,184
Ramyun is actually called "Secret ramyun."

1014
00:33:17,184 --> 00:33:19,643
Ramyun tastes best
when you eat it in secret.

1015
00:33:19,643 --> 00:33:21,473
We're gonna eat it in secret
when no one's watching or filming.

1016
00:33:21,473 --> 00:33:23,565
This is a build-up
for when you eat it all alone, huh?

1017
00:33:23,565 --> 00:33:25,744
I don't really like ramyun.

1018
00:33:25,744 --> 00:33:28,299
- Wanna play for all the ramyun?
- No.

1019
00:33:28,299 --> 00:33:30,072
But from what I heard earlier,

1020
00:33:30,072 --> 00:33:31,860
[Getting suspected of something weird]
Shin Dong eats one,

1021
00:33:31,860 --> 00:33:33,582
(1 ramyun / 1 ramyun for two)
and these two share one?

1022
00:33:33,582 --> 00:33:34,871
[We're gonna share it fairly]
But we have 3 ramyuns.

1023
00:33:34,871 --> 00:33:37,127
- Oh!
- They switched one for the Kimchi.

1024
00:33:37,127 --> 00:33:38,128
We can each have one.

1025
00:33:38,128 --> 00:33:39,394
Did you go for a walk, too?

1026
00:33:39,394 --> 00:33:40,461
- Yes!
- Yes.

1027
00:33:40,461 --> 00:33:44,044
[Enjoying a rare moment of peace]
You spent a very relaxing time. How was it?

1028
00:33:44,044 --> 00:33:45,577
I'm nervous.

1029
00:33:45,577 --> 00:33:47,367
[Always suspicious]
Why do you keep giving us these moments?

1030
00:33:47,367 --> 00:33:48,674
We don't have time.

1031
00:33:48,674 --> 00:33:50,689
Can I make this kind of suggestion?

1032
00:33:50,689 --> 00:33:52,217
Let's just be happy today

1033
00:33:52,217 --> 00:33:55,078
[Just for today, everyone's a prince?!]
with all 6 of us living the prince's life..!

1034
00:33:55,078 --> 00:33:57,645
(Good job, Shin Dong)
We need those kinds of moments.

1035
00:33:57,645 --> 00:33:59,356
- Exactly!
- Yeah, yeah!

1036
00:33:59,356 --> 00:34:01,810
- We're almost to the end now, right?
- That's right.

1037
00:34:01,810 --> 00:34:04,357
The title of this mission is…

1038
00:34:04,357 --> 00:34:06,362
"Conversations with the Ancients".

1039
00:34:06,362 --> 00:34:08,376
"Conversations with the Ancients"?

1040
00:34:08,376 --> 00:34:09,444
Is it a riddle?

1041
00:34:09,444 --> 00:34:13,110
Since you're living
in Egypt as princes or paupers,

1042
00:34:13,110 --> 00:34:15,530
[Egyptian princes]
as princes, you need to know the history…

1043
00:34:15,530 --> 00:34:19,062
as well as understand what kind of
communication took place in ancient times.

1044
00:34:19,062 --> 00:34:22,377
[So for this mission,]
We prepared a mission called "Conversations with the Ancients".

1045
00:34:22,377 --> 00:34:23,986
This mission is

1046
00:34:23,986 --> 00:34:24,977
a status mission!

1047
00:34:24,977 --> 00:34:25,994
[A status mission]
Oh…

1048
00:34:25,994 --> 00:34:27,067
Wait!

1049
00:34:27,067 --> 00:34:29,086
If it's about the ancients, isn't it that?
Like the hieroglyphics we saw.

1050
00:34:29,086 --> 00:34:29,986
- Oh!
- Yeah.

1051
00:34:29,986 --> 00:34:31,376
That's right.

1052
00:34:31,376 --> 00:34:33,909
[Two nights ago at Luxor Temple]
There are murals on the walls too.

1053
00:34:34,290 --> 00:34:35,377
[WANGGEOZ]
Yeah, there's something there.

1054
00:34:35,377 --> 00:34:37,265
[Discovered ancient hieroglyphics]
This is all text, right?

1055
00:34:37,265 --> 00:34:38,753
That's right.

1056
00:34:38,753 --> 00:34:39,787
Wow, Shin Dong!

1057
00:34:39,787 --> 00:34:42,882
[There's probably a decoding mission]
Something like searching this up and decoding it.

1058
00:34:42,882 --> 00:34:44,574
(Reasonable suspicion)
That's totally possible.

1059
00:34:46,074 --> 00:34:48,244
[What is it…?]
Do we have to find something?

1060
00:34:48,244 --> 00:34:50,510
This mission
doesn't have a long explanation.

1061
00:34:50,510 --> 00:34:52,892
The mission starts
as soon as I hand these to you.

1062
00:34:52,892 --> 00:34:54,273
First…

1063
00:34:54,273 --> 00:34:55,403
- Oh…!
- It's a solo battle.

1064
00:34:55,403 --> 00:34:56,777
[Solo battle]
Oh.

1065
00:34:56,777 --> 00:34:57,875
[Anxiety creeps in]
Oh, this is gonna be hard.

1066
00:34:57,875 --> 00:34:58,962
Ugh! I'm in trouble.

1067
00:34:58,962 --> 00:34:59,879
- I'm really bad at things like this.
- It's a solo battle, and…

1068
00:34:59,879 --> 00:35:02,674
[Prince status]
This time, the prince status will be given

1069
00:35:02,674 --> 00:35:03,377
[Only 2 people]
to only 2 people.

1070
00:35:03,377 --> 00:35:04,677
- Oh!
- What?

1071
00:35:04,677 --> 00:35:06,277
[Not 3 but 2?]
Is there another category for 1 person?

1072
00:35:06,277 --> 00:35:08,083
No, only 2 people will become princes…

1073
00:35:08,083 --> 00:35:10,453
- So, 4 paupers?
- 4 people will become paupers.

1074
00:35:10,453 --> 00:35:13,873
- We have 10 rooms on this island.
- Yes.

1075
00:35:13,873 --> 00:35:16,769
The 2 best rooms
will go to the princes.

1076
00:35:16,769 --> 00:35:18,677
[The exact rooms they called dibs on earlier]
Hey, I have to be a prince today.

1077
00:35:18,677 --> 00:35:20,977
If I become a prince,
I want room number 4.

1078
00:35:20,977 --> 00:35:22,444
Come on! That's not right!

1079
00:35:22,444 --> 00:35:24,277
[There are still 8 rooms left...]
Hey, there are rooms left over.

1080
00:35:24,277 --> 00:35:28,544
The 8 remaining rooms
will be given to the staff.

1081
00:35:28,544 --> 00:35:29,977
- Come on!
- Seriously, just 2 people?

1082
00:35:29,977 --> 00:35:31,410
Our equipment has to get charged and stuff.

1083
00:35:31,410 --> 00:35:32,610
The staff needs to freshen up as well.

1084
00:35:32,610 --> 00:35:34,168
[Then what about us…]
We also need to recharge.

1085
00:35:34,168 --> 00:35:35,810
- We need to recharge, too!
- But we have no place to recharge!

1086
00:35:35,810 --> 00:35:38,109
- This is quality TV!
- This is so great!

1087
00:35:39,376 --> 00:35:41,310
Your "This is so great"
came out so nasally.

1088
00:35:41,310 --> 00:35:42,509
This is so great!

1089
00:35:44,309 --> 00:35:46,058
[For the mission]
We'll be handing out

1090
00:35:46,058 --> 00:35:47,744
notebooks and pens to each of you.

1091
00:35:47,744 --> 00:35:50,074
[Notebooks and pens]
Don't open them until I say so.

1092
00:35:50,074 --> 00:35:50,994
Oh, don't open them?

1093
00:35:50,994 --> 00:35:53,582
Is this the famous
"PD Note" I've heard about?

1094
00:35:53,582 --> 00:35:54,731
[Heh]

1095
00:35:54,731 --> 00:35:56,277
[Not "PD Note"]
Everyone, take a "PD Note" each.

1096
00:35:56,277 --> 00:35:57,467
[Mystery notebooks are handed out]
Oh, I'm curious about this.

1097
00:35:57,467 --> 00:35:58,735
I almost opened it out of habit.

1098
00:35:58,735 --> 00:36:00,383
[What's written inside…?]
Hey, don't open it yet.

1099
00:36:00,383 --> 00:36:02,117
It's got that production vibe.

1100
00:36:02,566 --> 00:36:04,188
[Once it's open, it's game on!]
The moment you flip open the first page,

1101
00:36:04,188 --> 00:36:05,775
you can start right away.

1102
00:36:05,775 --> 00:36:06,677
Start right away?

1103
00:36:06,677 --> 00:36:08,582
- Yes, go ahead and open it.
- Open it?

1104
00:36:17,468 --> 00:36:21,477
"Obtain the clue next to
a big pool of fresh water."

1105
00:36:21,477 --> 00:36:25,177
"The one who finds and understands
the ancient language will become a prince."

1106
00:36:25,177 --> 00:36:29,377
"Blessings await those
who bring 'that' to the highest hut."

1107
00:36:29,377 --> 00:36:34,276
"The one who uses modern civilization
will beg for eternity."

1108
00:36:35,343 --> 00:36:40,210
[Conversations with the Ancients]

1109
00:36:40,210 --> 00:36:42,077
[The mission site is the whole island]

1110
00:36:42,077 --> 00:36:44,976
[Introducing key spots]

1111
00:36:46,309 --> 00:36:49,209
[The building at the very top of the island]

1112
00:36:49,209 --> 00:36:51,476
[with rooms for the princes]

1113
00:36:51,876 --> 00:36:54,443
[and a dining area]

1114
00:36:54,816 --> 00:36:57,283
[is the resort]

1115
00:36:57,709 --> 00:37:01,343
[If you follow the path
down from the resort…]

1116
00:37:01,809 --> 00:37:04,636
[The swimming pool]

1117
00:37:04,636 --> 00:37:09,169
[And 107 parasols dotting the island]

1118
00:37:09,709 --> 00:37:12,176
[To become a prince in this place today…?]

1119
00:37:12,609 --> 00:37:14,476
I feel like there's a catch…!

1120
00:37:16,573 --> 00:37:18,269
[Prince Qualification 1.]
I got it! I just need to find it now.

1121
00:37:18,269 --> 00:37:19,981
[Instinct: Trust your gut]
I just feel like there's something over there.

1122
00:37:19,981 --> 00:37:21,487
Oh, but I think this is it!

1123
00:37:21,487 --> 00:37:22,283
I found it!

1124
00:37:22,283 --> 00:37:23,877
- Oh…! Oh!!
- What is it?

1125
00:37:23,877 --> 00:37:25,198
What is it? What?
Hold on, what is it?

1126
00:37:25,198 --> 00:37:26,182
[Prince Qualification 2.]
There must be something there!

1127
00:37:26,182 --> 00:37:27,473
[Speed: Run like crazy]
I need to go over there! This can't wait!

1128
00:37:27,473 --> 00:37:28,510
I'll really tell you one.

1129
00:37:28,510 --> 00:37:29,898
There's one
all the way at the end.

1130
00:37:29,898 --> 00:37:31,377
[Prince Qualification 3. See through the lies]
Is he lying to me because he didn't find it?

1131
00:37:31,377 --> 00:37:33,777
- You're lying, huh?
- Then, that means someone lied.

1132
00:37:33,777 --> 00:37:34,744
Let's be princes.

1133
00:37:34,744 --> 00:37:35,477
There are 2 of us. 2!

1134
00:37:35,477 --> 00:37:36,410
Can I just team up with you?

1135
00:37:36,410 --> 00:37:38,544
[Is betrayal allowed?]
Can we form teams?

1136
00:37:38,544 --> 00:37:39,410
Am I the fool here?

1137
00:37:39,410 --> 00:37:40,310
[I'll help you]
I wanna give you the answer.

1138
00:37:40,310 --> 00:37:41,010
[Don't trust that]
That's not it.

1139
00:37:41,010 --> 00:37:42,174
[There's no one to trust]
I can't trust anyone now.

1140
00:37:42,174 --> 00:37:43,548
I'm doomed.

1141
00:37:44,165 --> 00:37:45,177
[Sorry, but...]
Sorry.

1142
00:37:45,177 --> 00:37:46,468
[The right to be a prince belongs to me]
I really need to…

1143
00:37:46,468 --> 00:37:48,073
I really need
to be a prince this time.

1144
00:37:48,073 --> 00:37:49,057
[Only two prince spots]
Hurry up!

1145
00:37:49,057 --> 00:37:50,562
This is seriously driving me crazy.

1146
00:37:50,562 --> 00:37:52,390
- No! This isn't right!
- What? What? What?

1147
00:37:52,390 --> 00:37:53,977
Oh, please, please!

1148
00:37:53,977 --> 00:37:55,893
[The status mission]
I really wanna be a prince.

1149
00:37:55,893 --> 00:37:58,476
[will begin now]
I'm gonna be a prince

1150
00:37:58,476 --> 00:38:00,550
"The one who uses
modern civilization…"

1151
00:38:00,550 --> 00:38:01,280
[Whoosh]

1152
00:38:01,280 --> 00:38:03,343
"will beg for eternity."

1153
00:38:03,343 --> 00:38:06,864
[Leaving before reading it all]

1154
00:38:06,864 --> 00:38:08,663
- "Blessings await those…"
- Can we go now?

1155
00:38:08,663 --> 00:38:11,109
[Dash]
"who bring 'that' to the highest hut."

1156
00:38:11,109 --> 00:38:13,543
[Darted off first,
even leaving his assigned camera behind]

1157
00:38:14,276 --> 00:38:17,743
[Dash]

1158
00:38:20,035 --> 00:38:22,869
[And the 3 who haven't left yet]
A big pool of fresh water.

1159
00:38:22,869 --> 00:38:23,882
Fresh water?

1160
00:38:23,882 --> 00:38:25,077
[Fresh water...?]
What's "fresh water"?

1161
00:38:25,077 --> 00:38:27,065
What's "fresh water"?

1162
00:38:28,040 --> 00:38:29,864
- We should know what it is before we go.
- Fresh water, fresh water, hold on.

1163
00:38:29,864 --> 00:38:31,603
[Sorry, we didn't think you wouldn't know]
I don't know it either. Can I look it up?

1164
00:38:31,603 --> 00:38:34,244
You're not gonna tell me?
"Fresh water" and a "pool"?

1165
00:38:34,244 --> 00:38:35,610
You know what a pool is.

1166
00:38:35,610 --> 00:38:36,544
I really don't know.

1167
00:38:36,544 --> 00:38:38,643
I know what a "butt" is.

1168
00:38:39,670 --> 00:38:41,286
[Another person who doesn't know what "fresh water" is]
Where's the fresh water?

1169
00:38:41,286 --> 00:38:43,133
You gotta find it.

1170
00:38:43,133 --> 00:38:47,543
"A big pool of fresh water."

1171
00:38:47,543 --> 00:38:50,409
[Let's just go down first]

1172
00:38:50,876 --> 00:38:52,677
What's "fresh water"?

1173
00:38:52,677 --> 00:38:54,466
[Staff's inner thoughts]
Anyone know what fresh water is?

1174
00:38:54,466 --> 00:38:57,669
[Oh no…We didn't think of this scenario]
Fresh water…

1175
00:38:57,669 --> 00:39:00,043
Fresh... fresh... fresh.

1176
00:39:00,043 --> 00:39:02,164
"A big pool of fresh water."

1177
00:39:02,164 --> 00:39:05,276
Fresh water. Is this talking about a pool?

1178
00:39:05,276 --> 00:39:08,209
[Is the fresh water a pool?]
Isn't it a pool?

1179
00:39:08,676 --> 00:39:11,076
[First to arrive at the pool]

1180
00:39:11,509 --> 00:39:13,371
[A big pool of fresh water]
Where's the clue? Where's the clue?

1181
00:39:13,371 --> 00:39:15,609
[Immediately thought of the pool]

1182
00:39:15,609 --> 00:39:19,609
[Is the clue nearby?]

1183
00:39:20,077 --> 00:39:22,777
"A biiig butt of fresh water…"

1184
00:39:22,777 --> 00:39:25,309
A big pool!

1185
00:39:25,309 --> 00:39:28,076
[Shin Dong heads to the pool too]

1186
00:39:28,076 --> 00:39:29,076
[The "pool" is difficult for Chicago Guy]
What's a "pool"?

1187
00:39:29,076 --> 00:39:31,976
Just follow the others for now.

1188
00:39:31,976 --> 00:39:33,677
[The pool]
Oh, it's exactly that.

1189
00:39:33,677 --> 00:39:36,276
But that seems way too easy.

1190
00:39:36,276 --> 00:39:37,544
- DAWN!
- Yeah.

1191
00:39:37,544 --> 00:39:38,964
What's "fresh water"?

1192
00:39:38,964 --> 00:39:40,077
[Fresh water]
"Fresh water" is…

1193
00:39:40,077 --> 00:39:41,179
[Like a river or a lake]
It's probably water. Water.

1194
00:39:41,179 --> 00:39:42,168
[Water without salt. = Fresh water]

1195
00:39:42,168 --> 00:39:43,177
And a "pool"?

1196
00:39:43,177 --> 00:39:44,680
[Pool]
A pool is basically filled with water…

1197
00:39:44,680 --> 00:39:45,780
[A sunken spot where water collects.]
It's kind of like a pond.

1198
00:39:45,780 --> 00:39:46,577
[Much smaller than a swamp.]

1199
00:39:46,577 --> 00:39:51,658
[Most likely spot: Swimming pool]
So, actually, that swimming pool is the most likely…!

1200
00:39:51,658 --> 00:39:54,377
If I have to solve
these one by one…

1201
00:39:54,377 --> 00:40:00,310
"Next to a big pool of fresh water."

1202
00:40:00,310 --> 00:40:02,177
Next to a big pool!

1203
00:40:02,177 --> 00:40:03,709
Next To!

1204
00:40:07,281 --> 00:40:09,109
I came here with the mission!

1205
00:40:09,109 --> 00:40:10,176
[Jump]

1206
00:40:10,909 --> 00:40:12,256
[First to get the clue]

1207
00:40:12,256 --> 00:40:13,456
Let's look at it together!

1208
00:40:13,456 --> 00:40:14,389
They can't run
all the way here yet.

1209
00:40:14,389 --> 00:40:15,571
- Together, together,
- We're 2 people! 2 people!

1210
00:40:15,571 --> 00:40:21,244
[Obtain the clue next to
a big pool of fresh water]

1211
00:40:21,244 --> 00:40:24,776
[You get a clue
if you go by the swimming pool]

1212
00:40:24,776 --> 00:40:25,777
[Shin Dong gets a clue too]

1213
00:40:25,777 --> 00:40:28,638
Okay!
So this is it.

1214
00:40:28,638 --> 00:40:30,877
[What's the clue that they got?]
So, what about this?

1215
00:40:30,877 --> 00:40:33,426
What am I supposed to do with this?

1216
00:40:35,243 --> 00:40:38,809
[After getting the clue,
he searches around the pool]

1217
00:40:38,809 --> 00:40:40,377
[DAWN joins them at the pool]

1218
00:40:40,377 --> 00:40:42,277
[Passed the clue pickup spot]
It's fresh water!

1219
00:40:42,277 --> 00:40:43,425
By the fresh water…!

1220
00:40:46,585 --> 00:40:47,873
[A crowd gathers near the pool]
Next to it.

1221
00:40:47,873 --> 00:40:50,771
- Are we not understanding this?
- A big pool.

1222
00:40:50,771 --> 00:40:53,277
[Chicago Hot Guy's Korean class]
This is the big pool.

1223
00:40:53,277 --> 00:40:55,676
Next to it?

1224
00:40:56,490 --> 00:40:59,043
Huh? Over there…?

1225
00:40:59,576 --> 00:41:02,077
[Even the eldest who came to the beachside]
Is it there?

1226
00:41:02,077 --> 00:41:03,377
[changes direction
to the pool, where the crowd is]

1227
00:41:03,377 --> 00:41:04,844
Yeah.

1228
00:41:04,844 --> 00:41:06,877
That could be it.

1229
00:41:06,877 --> 00:41:08,271
If we're going down,
we're going down together

1230
00:41:08,271 --> 00:41:09,492
I'm too nervous. I can't do this.

1231
00:41:09,492 --> 00:41:11,409
If we're going down,
we're going down together

1232
00:41:15,343 --> 00:41:16,343
Huh??

1233
00:41:16,856 --> 00:41:18,576
- Huh?
- No way!

1234
00:41:20,076 --> 00:41:21,744
He's lying. Such a lie!

1235
00:41:21,744 --> 00:41:22,910
You can't pass!

1236
00:41:22,910 --> 00:41:25,309
I'm just kidding.

1237
00:41:25,309 --> 00:41:27,343
Hey, do you see something there?!

1238
00:41:29,209 --> 00:41:31,477
[inaudible]
It must be there. Ugh, I'm doomed.

1239
00:41:31,477 --> 00:41:32,909
I'm doomed, totally doomed!

1240
00:41:33,376 --> 00:41:35,577
Hey, is there something there???!!!

1241
00:41:35,577 --> 00:41:36,577
There's nothing here!

1242
00:41:36,577 --> 00:41:38,809
Sorry, Lee Teuk.
There's nothing here.

1243
00:41:38,809 --> 00:41:41,277
Is this the fresh water?

1244
00:41:41,277 --> 00:41:43,078
I feel like it wouldn't be this easy.

1245
00:41:43,078 --> 00:41:44,376
Yeah.

1246
00:41:44,376 --> 00:41:46,243
A pool…

1247
00:41:48,869 --> 00:41:50,398
(Must make eye contact to get the clue)
[Johnny also gets the clue]

1248
00:41:50,398 --> 00:41:51,566
Suddenly…

1249
00:41:51,566 --> 00:41:54,509
[Lee Teuk and DAWN still have no clue]
Did I get it right?

1250
00:41:55,394 --> 00:41:57,377
Why did you give me this?

1251
00:41:57,377 --> 00:42:00,443
[What clue did Johnny get?]
Did I do something good?

1252
00:42:02,576 --> 00:42:07,076
[Egyptian hieroglyphics / English alphabet]

1253
00:42:07,809 --> 00:42:11,277
(Sold at the market)
[Ancient Egypt hieroglyph decoder]

1254
00:42:11,277 --> 00:42:12,977
When I got the decoder,

1255
00:42:12,977 --> 00:42:15,876
I immediately thought,
"I just need to find these characters"

1256
00:42:17,575 --> 00:42:18,568
Oh!

1257
00:42:19,857 --> 00:42:20,750
So,

1258
00:42:21,472 --> 00:42:23,943
I have to find something
that looks like this!

1259
00:42:24,380 --> 00:42:26,876
[Moving while holding the decoder]
I have to find something that looks like this.

1260
00:42:26,876 --> 00:42:29,910
[These hieroglyphics are hidden
somewhere on the island]

1261
00:42:29,910 --> 00:42:30,977
[Status of Decoder Holders]

1262
00:42:30,977 --> 00:42:32,477
[Obtained]
[Shin Dong / Johnny / Ji Sung]

1263
00:42:32,477 --> 00:42:33,976
[Not obtained]
[Lee Teuk / DAWN / Yo Han]

1264
00:42:33,976 --> 00:42:37,577
[While everyone's
focused on the fresh water,]

1265
00:42:37,577 --> 00:42:41,809
[there's one guy
who chose to go a different path alone]

1266
00:42:41,809 --> 00:42:43,809
[Looking around]

1267
00:42:45,409 --> 00:42:48,309
[Spotting a suspicious area along the shore]

1268
00:42:50,843 --> 00:42:54,209
[Entering like he's under a spell]

1269
00:42:56,543 --> 00:42:59,476
[Yo Han, who was
wandering alone, had a thought]

1270
00:43:00,343 --> 00:43:03,377
A different… Very…

1271
00:43:03,377 --> 00:43:06,009
I'm barking up the wrong tree, huh?

1272
00:43:07,109 --> 00:43:11,476
[Type to just charge right in]

1273
00:43:12,009 --> 00:43:13,977
[Frustrated]

1274
00:43:13,977 --> 00:43:15,815
Ugh, seriously.

1275
00:43:16,876 --> 00:43:19,176
How am I supposed
to find the clues?

1276
00:43:19,176 --> 00:43:20,609
[Looking around]

1277
00:43:20,994 --> 00:43:24,776
[But his gut keeps pointing here]
It feels like something's here.

1278
00:43:28,816 --> 00:43:31,073
Wow! This is bad!

1279
00:43:31,073 --> 00:43:32,563
I'm in big trouble!

1280
00:43:32,563 --> 00:43:33,309
An eagle.

1281
00:43:33,309 --> 00:43:35,479
[Found a mysterious eagle drawing]

1282
00:43:35,479 --> 00:43:36,476
An eagle.

1283
00:43:37,575 --> 00:43:38,779
An eagle.

1284
00:43:39,709 --> 00:43:44,376
[Jotting it down before he forgets]

1285
00:43:46,509 --> 00:43:50,276
[Found something important
that's clearly suspicious]

1286
00:43:50,276 --> 00:43:53,109
[Checking the mission sheet again]

1287
00:43:53,109 --> 00:43:55,101
"The highest hut"?

1288
00:43:55,878 --> 00:43:58,309
[Next target]
"The highest hut"?

1289
00:44:00,572 --> 00:44:01,667
Oh, it's that!

1290
00:44:01,667 --> 00:44:03,286
It's that, it's that!

1291
00:44:04,601 --> 00:44:07,177
"The highest hut"?

1292
00:44:07,177 --> 00:44:08,976
Is this not it?

1293
00:44:09,509 --> 00:44:12,809
[Is it not…?]

1294
00:44:13,309 --> 00:44:15,709
[Ssp…]
Someone's doing something here.

1295
00:44:17,176 --> 00:44:18,177
Why is everyone hiding, though?

1296
00:44:18,177 --> 00:44:20,056
It has to be here.

1297
00:44:20,056 --> 00:44:22,770
Is it not here?

1298
00:44:22,770 --> 00:44:24,776
[Just staff members…]
It's not? It's not? Oh.

1299
00:44:24,776 --> 00:44:28,143
[Back to searching for the highest hut]

1300
00:44:28,776 --> 00:44:32,243
[The highest hut…]

1301
00:44:32,967 --> 00:44:35,036
Where's the highest hut?

1302
00:44:35,036 --> 00:44:36,768
[The highest hut is]
Is it not here?

1303
00:44:36,768 --> 00:44:38,176
[at the highest place]

1304
00:44:39,756 --> 00:44:42,509
Is that the highest hut?

1305
00:44:42,509 --> 00:44:45,209
[Since I spotted it,
I need to go over there]

1306
00:44:45,209 --> 00:44:47,477
[Climb up the hill]

1307
00:44:47,477 --> 00:44:51,176
[And keep climbing
and you'll get there]

1308
00:44:51,176 --> 00:44:53,476
The highest hut!

1309
00:44:53,476 --> 00:44:54,644
It's here.

1310
00:44:54,644 --> 00:44:56,877
[The highest hut: Arrived at HQ]
Did you find it?

1311
00:44:56,877 --> 00:44:58,377
Please hand over what you found.

1312
00:44:58,377 --> 00:45:00,343
[Clue]
[Handed over the hieroglyph decoder]

1313
00:45:01,076 --> 00:45:02,510
[Nope. Go back]
This isn't it.

1314
00:45:02,510 --> 00:45:03,477
It's not this?

1315
00:45:03,477 --> 00:45:06,143
You have to find it using this.

1316
00:45:06,676 --> 00:45:09,509
[Find it using this??]

1317
00:45:09,509 --> 00:45:11,777
This isn't the clue,

1318
00:45:11,777 --> 00:45:13,776
but there's something else.

1319
00:45:13,776 --> 00:45:16,809
There must be another piece of paper…

1320
00:45:16,809 --> 00:45:19,842
[Meanwhile, Yo Han spots an eagle]

1321
00:45:19,842 --> 00:45:23,909
[Yo Han's biggest strength: Endless stamina]

1322
00:45:24,570 --> 00:45:26,233
But where exactly?

1323
00:45:26,233 --> 00:45:27,170
Go this way for now?

1324
00:45:27,170 --> 00:45:28,936
[Sprinting to the highest hut]

1325
00:45:29,309 --> 00:45:31,843
[Cleared the hill in one go
with his insane physical power]

1326
00:45:33,343 --> 00:45:35,043
The highest hut!

1327
00:45:35,043 --> 00:45:36,577
Did you bring it?

1328
00:45:36,577 --> 00:45:39,043
I heard it's for everyone to share?

1329
00:45:39,493 --> 00:45:40,667
What is it?

1330
00:45:41,176 --> 00:45:43,277
The clue…!

1331
00:45:43,277 --> 00:45:44,310
It's not the clue?

1332
00:45:44,310 --> 00:45:46,744
["The ancient language" / What Yo Han found]
Based on the clue,

1333
00:45:46,744 --> 00:45:48,976
you have to find that item.

1334
00:45:48,976 --> 00:45:52,777
[So the eagle wasn't the answer...]
Sigh.

1335
00:45:52,777 --> 00:45:56,444
When I read the text,
I honestly didn't understand it.

1336
00:45:56,444 --> 00:45:59,409
How do I even find this…?

1337
00:45:59,835 --> 00:46:02,382
[Didn't get the crucial clue, the decoder]
I found the clue, but…

1338
00:46:02,382 --> 00:46:03,750
The eagle.

1339
00:46:04,474 --> 00:46:06,609
This is driving me crazy...!

1340
00:46:06,609 --> 00:46:09,643
Let's think about it…

1341
00:46:09,643 --> 00:46:11,844
[3 seconds later]

1342
00:46:11,844 --> 00:46:14,244
I have no idea.

1343
00:46:14,244 --> 00:46:16,677
[Hop! Hop!]
[Ji Sung's collection status: Nothing]

1344
00:46:16,677 --> 00:46:18,110
[Pitter-patter]

1345
00:46:18,110 --> 00:46:21,209
[Ji Sung just dashes off without thinking]

1346
00:46:21,843 --> 00:46:23,643
[To the camera director]
Hello!

1347
00:46:24,443 --> 00:46:27,343
[He ran around, but with no luck]
Ugh, this is exhausting.

1348
00:46:28,809 --> 00:46:29,777
39?!

1349
00:46:29,777 --> 00:46:30,938
What is this?

1350
00:46:31,676 --> 00:46:33,598
I don't think it's anything…

1351
00:46:40,143 --> 00:46:43,176
[First mysterious paper found]

1352
00:46:43,176 --> 00:46:45,576
[What is this...?]

1353
00:46:46,876 --> 00:46:48,243
Huh?

1354
00:46:49,243 --> 00:46:50,654
Is this right?

1355
00:46:50,654 --> 00:46:53,154
[Just a drink menu]
It's the name of things on the menu.

1356
00:46:55,409 --> 00:46:58,290
Huh? Why is my phone here?!

1357
00:46:58,290 --> 00:47:00,576
I was here earlier during our break.

1358
00:47:00,576 --> 00:47:05,176
[Current status]
[Acquired his phone + a menu]

1359
00:47:06,509 --> 00:47:08,709
Find the pool! The pool!

1360
00:47:09,243 --> 00:47:12,877
[Lee Teuk's Collection Status: Nothing]

1361
00:47:12,877 --> 00:47:15,709
[Still searching near the fresh water]

1362
00:47:16,643 --> 00:47:18,010
Fresh water...

1363
00:47:18,010 --> 00:47:20,010
A butt filled with fresh water.

1364
00:47:20,010 --> 00:47:22,543
A pool, not a butt,
but a pool of water.

1365
00:47:22,543 --> 00:47:25,476
[An endless freshwater pool loop]

1366
00:47:25,476 --> 00:47:27,843
"next to a big pool of fresh water…"

1367
00:47:30,509 --> 00:47:31,925
[Like a skit, Johnny appears]

1368
00:47:31,925 --> 00:47:32,969
Did you find anything?

1369
00:47:32,969 --> 00:47:35,329
- Hey, where'd you get that?
- Uh, Oh!

1370
00:47:35,329 --> 00:47:36,010
Where did you get that?

1371
00:47:36,010 --> 00:47:37,898
- You didn't get one?
- Yeah.

1372
00:47:37,898 --> 00:47:38,702
[Decoder]
Where did you get that?

1373
00:47:38,702 --> 00:47:39,837
[Why do only you have it?]
No idea.

1374
00:47:39,837 --> 00:47:41,484
What?

1375
00:47:41,484 --> 00:47:43,701
- Hey, where'd you pick that up?
- Huh?

1376
00:47:43,701 --> 00:47:45,743
- Where did you get it??
- I really don't know...

1377
00:47:45,743 --> 00:47:47,777
Honestly, I still don't know
why I got it either.

1378
00:47:47,777 --> 00:47:49,477
- Did they give it to you?
- Yeah.

1379
00:47:49,477 --> 00:47:50,866
[Feeling left out]
Why? Why didn't I get one?

1380
00:47:50,866 --> 00:47:52,277
As I said, I have no clue either.

1381
00:47:52,277 --> 00:47:54,709
Why???

1382
00:47:55,368 --> 00:47:57,951
- I really don't know.
- Is that the clue?

1383
00:47:57,951 --> 00:47:58,719
I have no idea.

1384
00:47:58,719 --> 00:47:59,868
[Let's look at it together]
Let me see!

1385
00:47:59,868 --> 00:48:01,777
- I honestly wouldn't even if I looked.
- Yeah.

1386
00:48:01,777 --> 00:48:04,076
It's just A, B, C, D.

1387
00:48:04,076 --> 00:48:05,777
Why didn't I get one?

1388
00:48:05,777 --> 00:48:08,832
If you go to
the clue's location, you can find out.

1389
00:48:08,832 --> 00:48:09,867
Isn't it the pool? The fresh water?

1390
00:48:09,867 --> 00:48:11,476
Everyone went there earlier.

1391
00:48:13,403 --> 00:48:16,576
[Why didn't I get one...
What's the reason...]

1392
00:48:16,576 --> 00:48:20,609
[Bracing himself and sprinting]

1393
00:48:21,076 --> 00:48:23,409
[Heave-ho]

1394
00:48:25,557 --> 00:48:27,044
How come you're not
giving me a clue?!

1395
00:48:27,044 --> 00:48:28,582
[Waiting for the clue]

1396
00:48:28,582 --> 00:48:29,576
Oh, here…!

1397
00:48:29,576 --> 00:48:33,409
[Whiny Lee Teuk]
I was here earlier! Why didn't you give it to meee!

1398
00:48:34,172 --> 00:48:35,976
What am I supposed to do with this?

1399
00:48:36,543 --> 00:48:38,676
[What is it?]

1400
00:48:40,982 --> 00:48:43,982
[Yo Han also gets the hieroglyph decoder]
Let's take it slow.

1401
00:48:51,109 --> 00:48:55,176
[The first person
to figure out this mission]

1402
00:48:56,043 --> 00:48:57,809
A!!

1403
00:48:57,809 --> 00:48:59,077
It turns out

1404
00:48:59,077 --> 00:49:02,586
[The decoder]
the clue was next to the pool.

1405
00:49:02,586 --> 00:49:05,710
And the decoder
had the letter "A".

1406
00:49:05,710 --> 00:49:08,077
So, I had to find the pictures,
combine the letters together,

1407
00:49:08,077 --> 00:49:10,609
[= A]
and bring it back!

1408
00:49:10,609 --> 00:49:13,143
I lost...!

1409
00:49:13,143 --> 00:49:15,159
I'm not good at English...

1410
00:49:15,159 --> 00:49:17,982
I've only done sports
since I was a kid.

1411
00:49:18,376 --> 00:49:20,136
I'm not good at English.

1412
00:49:20,136 --> 00:49:24,144
[107 parasols]

1413
00:49:24,144 --> 00:49:28,243
[The ancient language
is hidden all over the island]

1414
00:49:28,243 --> 00:49:32,443
[Find and piece together
the ancient language]

1415
00:49:32,443 --> 00:49:36,144
[Bring "that" to the highest hut]

1416
00:49:36,144 --> 00:49:39,976
[Who will decode the ancient language?]

1417
00:49:40,443 --> 00:49:43,176
[Yo Han's collection status: A]

1418
00:49:43,176 --> 00:49:45,677
[Ran into DAWN while excitedly running around
after getting the language chart]

1419
00:49:45,677 --> 00:49:47,777
- DAWN, how many did you see?
- Huh?

1420
00:49:47,777 --> 00:49:49,777
DAWN, how many did you see?

1421
00:49:49,777 --> 00:49:50,943
You got the clue too, right?

1422
00:49:50,943 --> 00:49:52,162
- Huh? You got something?
- Yeah.

1423
00:49:52,162 --> 00:49:54,377
[Trying to trade info]
Should we swap clues?

1424
00:49:54,377 --> 00:49:57,148
Let's exchange clues.
We can both become princes.

1425
00:49:57,768 --> 00:49:58,877
I'll really tell you one.

1426
00:49:58,877 --> 00:50:01,209
I even drew it here.

1427
00:50:01,209 --> 00:50:03,764
[5 minutes ago, at the hut]

1428
00:50:03,764 --> 00:50:05,376
Oh!

1429
00:50:06,709 --> 00:50:09,676
[Spotted the eagle!]

1430
00:50:09,676 --> 00:50:11,477
Hold up, I need to sketch this out.

1431
00:50:11,477 --> 00:50:14,202
It might be hieroglyphics or something.

1432
00:50:14,202 --> 00:50:17,236
[Drawing the image
because he didn't get a decoder]

1433
00:50:17,236 --> 00:50:18,944
(Honest)
I even drew it here.

1434
00:50:18,944 --> 00:50:19,577
[An eagle]
I've got one too.

1435
00:50:19,577 --> 00:50:20,677
How many do you have?

1436
00:50:20,677 --> 00:50:22,010
Where did you see it?
Just tell me that.

1437
00:50:22,010 --> 00:50:24,177
[They both have the same info]
Come on, seriously.

1438
00:50:24,177 --> 00:50:26,944
[Revealing the decoder he just got]
You got this too, right?

1439
00:50:26,944 --> 00:50:28,477
[What's that...??]
Where'd you find that?

1440
00:50:28,477 --> 00:50:29,877
(Over…th…)

1441
00:50:29,877 --> 00:50:30,744
For real?

1442
00:50:30,744 --> 00:50:31,577
(Urgent)
DAWN! Hurry!

1443
00:50:31,577 --> 00:50:34,577
- Let's seriously share this.
- What did you see?

1444
00:50:34,577 --> 00:50:36,680
I swear I'll show you.
Let's make a promise!

1445
00:50:36,680 --> 00:50:37,743
Promise, promise!

1446
00:50:37,743 --> 00:50:38,877
(Nervous)
Oh, wait.

1447
00:50:38,877 --> 00:50:41,044
The 2 of us…!
Although it's a solo battle,

1448
00:50:41,044 --> 00:50:43,310
[You and me]
2 people can become princes!

1449
00:50:43,310 --> 00:50:45,876
I don't think I can.
But I think we saw the same thing.

1450
00:50:45,876 --> 00:50:46,887
No, it's not the same thing.

1451
00:50:46,887 --> 00:50:48,572
[Clue paper]
Nope, this is my first time seeing this.

1452
00:50:48,572 --> 00:50:50,144
[The decoder is the clue]
Oh, this is the language. The language!

1453
00:50:50,144 --> 00:50:52,038
[I'm the only one without it]
So, where did you get that language from?

1454
00:50:52,709 --> 00:50:54,484
[Secret]
I have no idea...

1455
00:50:54,484 --> 00:50:56,877
Seriously, let's share...

1456
00:50:56,877 --> 00:50:58,001
[Opening notebook amid distrust]
I'll really show you.

1457
00:50:58,001 --> 00:50:59,448
If you show me, I'll show you too.

1458
00:50:59,448 --> 00:51:00,576
Oh, it's the same.
The eagle.

1459
00:51:00,576 --> 00:51:01,504
- Oh.
- I saw an eagle, too.

1460
00:51:01,504 --> 00:51:03,549
Then, where did you get that?

1461
00:51:03,549 --> 00:51:05,210
- That's kind of…
- What's the eagle?

1462
00:51:05,210 --> 00:51:06,799
[They just give it to you if you go there…]
Come on!

1463
00:51:06,799 --> 00:51:07,572
Hey!

1464
00:51:07,572 --> 00:51:09,410
- No! This isn't right!
- What? What? What?

1465
00:51:09,410 --> 00:51:10,376
- Ji Sung!
- Yes!

1466
00:51:10,376 --> 00:51:12,809
Where did you get
that "Ancient Language Chart"?

1467
00:51:12,809 --> 00:51:13,977
This is a menu.

1468
00:51:13,977 --> 00:51:15,077
No, I mean that Ancient Language Chart.

1469
00:51:15,077 --> 00:51:15,977
[Sharing it right away]
Near the pool!

1470
00:51:15,977 --> 00:51:17,109
Oh, okay, okay.

1471
00:51:17,109 --> 00:51:19,076
[Thanks for the kindness, Ji Sung]

1472
00:51:19,576 --> 00:51:22,409
[Dashing straight to the pool]

1473
00:51:25,043 --> 00:51:26,944
Is this where we get the decoder?

1474
00:51:26,944 --> 00:51:29,344
[All members receive the hieroglyph decoder]

1475
00:51:29,344 --> 00:51:32,309
[DAWN also secures an "A"]
A.

1476
00:51:32,309 --> 00:51:34,147
[Still "pooling" around, he returns to the pool]
The pool.

1477
00:51:34,147 --> 00:51:35,443
The pool?

1478
00:51:35,443 --> 00:51:36,876
Shin Dong, how many have you found?

1479
00:51:36,876 --> 00:51:39,309
How many have I found?

1480
00:51:39,309 --> 00:51:41,209
[Oh, you didn't know]

1481
00:51:41,209 --> 00:51:44,276
How many have I found?

1482
00:51:44,276 --> 00:51:46,677
[Obtained info that there are many]
How many?

1483
00:51:46,677 --> 00:51:48,886
[The biiig pool time returns]
"Obtain the clue next to"

1484
00:51:48,886 --> 00:51:49,844
[An endless loop]
"a big pool of freshwater."

1485
00:51:49,844 --> 00:51:52,176
"The one who finds and understands
the ancient language will become a prince."

1486
00:51:55,176 --> 00:51:58,209
[Where is everyone finding them?]

1487
00:51:58,809 --> 00:52:01,809
There's nothing here.
Why haven't I found anything?

1488
00:52:04,576 --> 00:52:06,876
Wow, I think I'm doomed.

1489
00:52:07,776 --> 00:52:10,309
Am I the only one
who can't see anything?

1490
00:52:10,309 --> 00:52:13,176
[Ji Sung searches
through parasols like crazy]

1491
00:52:15,876 --> 00:52:18,443
I don't think this is it.

1492
00:52:19,676 --> 00:52:20,676
Huh?

1493
00:52:21,249 --> 00:52:26,549
[Eagle "A" spotted!]

1494
00:52:30,043 --> 00:52:32,410
[Oh, so that's how you do it!]

1495
00:52:32,410 --> 00:52:35,276
The faster I go,
the sooner I get first place!

1496
00:52:35,276 --> 00:52:36,610
I'll find them quickly…!

1497
00:52:36,610 --> 00:52:38,343
And be at an advantage!

1498
00:52:45,776 --> 00:52:48,943
[Found the lion drawing]

1499
00:52:48,943 --> 00:52:51,176
[The second letter, "L"]

1500
00:52:53,909 --> 00:52:55,044
Ji Sung, did you see anything?

1501
00:52:55,044 --> 00:52:56,644
[Found 2]
Me? Nope, I really didn't see a thing

1502
00:52:56,644 --> 00:52:57,844
What did the others find?

1503
00:52:57,844 --> 00:53:00,977
[Playing dumb]
No idea... I don't know at all.

1504
00:53:00,977 --> 00:53:02,877
Heheh...

1505
00:53:02,877 --> 00:53:05,410
Sorry, Lee Teuk…

1506
00:53:05,410 --> 00:53:07,077
Today, I really…

1507
00:53:07,077 --> 00:53:09,220
I really need
to be a prince this time!

1508
00:53:10,076 --> 00:53:11,877
[Sprinting]

1509
00:53:11,877 --> 00:53:12,610
Hey, why are you…?

1510
00:53:12,610 --> 00:53:13,715
What are you doing?!!!

1511
00:53:13,715 --> 00:53:14,676
Where are you going?

1512
00:53:14,676 --> 00:53:17,343
Hey, why are you being like that?

1513
00:53:18,176 --> 00:53:20,243
(Quietly followed behind him)

1514
00:53:21,943 --> 00:53:24,376
[Owl spotted]

1515
00:53:24,376 --> 00:53:26,509
[Yo Han spots it too]

1516
00:53:26,509 --> 00:53:29,243
[Found the owl!]

1517
00:53:29,243 --> 00:53:31,609
[When you decode the owl,
you get an "M"]

1518
00:53:31,609 --> 00:53:34,903
[Letters uncovered so far]
["A", "L", "M"]

1519
00:53:34,903 --> 00:53:35,703
Hey!

1520
00:53:36,176 --> 00:53:38,377
Let's do that!
Let's share!

1521
00:53:38,377 --> 00:53:39,777
[Wasp booster ON]
Ji Sung!

1522
00:53:39,777 --> 00:53:41,361
Ji Sung!

1523
00:53:41,361 --> 00:53:42,743
I'm gonna be a prince!

1524
00:53:42,743 --> 00:53:45,235
Ji Sung, let's share just once!

1525
00:53:45,235 --> 00:53:47,576
How many did you find?

1526
00:53:47,576 --> 00:53:48,977
"A", "L", "M".

1527
00:53:48,977 --> 00:53:50,909
[Dash]

1528
00:53:50,909 --> 00:53:53,189
What's "A", "L", "M"?

1529
00:53:53,189 --> 00:53:56,746
["A", "L", "M"]
[Honestly shared and then dipped]

1530
00:53:56,746 --> 00:53:59,344
But does he not want to check mine?

1531
00:53:59,344 --> 00:54:02,476
He just left.

1532
00:54:04,269 --> 00:54:07,814
[The hieroglyphic for a lion]
"L"…?

1533
00:54:07,814 --> 00:54:08,976
A lion.

1534
00:54:08,976 --> 00:54:11,143
I think I know it!

1535
00:54:13,143 --> 00:54:16,043
So, it's not just random running.

1536
00:54:16,043 --> 00:54:19,276
[Looks like he found an epic shortcut]

1537
00:54:20,076 --> 00:54:21,777
[Analyzing the pattern
printed on the mission paper]

1538
00:54:21,777 --> 00:54:24,160
Slowly, slowly.
There's no need to rush.

1539
00:54:24,160 --> 00:54:26,022
You can do this.

1540
00:54:28,176 --> 00:54:32,543
But there's no fish?

1541
00:54:33,617 --> 00:54:35,543
Wow, this is really hard.

1542
00:54:35,543 --> 00:54:37,509
[Because that's not how it's done...]

1543
00:54:38,843 --> 00:54:42,309
[Johnny shows up like a skit again]
No one knows. It's okay. I can do it.

1544
00:54:45,643 --> 00:54:46,910
Did you find it?

1545
00:54:46,910 --> 00:54:49,476
No, I thought you found it.

1546
00:54:50,043 --> 00:54:52,743
I'm still looking.

1547
00:54:52,743 --> 00:54:54,477
Like, "Don't leave this area"?

1548
00:54:54,477 --> 00:54:55,677
Is there something like that?

1549
00:54:55,677 --> 00:54:57,909
[No restricted area]

1550
00:54:57,909 --> 00:54:59,087
That's the hut.

1551
00:54:59,087 --> 00:55:01,865
So, we just have
to get there in the end.

1552
00:55:01,865 --> 00:55:03,976
What am I supposed to interpret?

1553
00:55:04,569 --> 00:55:08,009
Oh, so I have to
find the ancient symbols right now.

1554
00:55:08,009 --> 00:55:11,443
[Realization while talking]
Oh, what? I'm such an idiot.

1555
00:55:11,443 --> 00:55:13,477
[Focusing]

1556
00:55:13,477 --> 00:55:16,020
There's definitely something here.

1557
00:55:17,376 --> 00:55:23,109
There's gotta be coordinates here…!

1558
00:55:23,109 --> 00:55:24,843
Oh!

1559
00:55:25,909 --> 00:55:30,575
Where could it be?

1560
00:55:31,155 --> 00:55:34,776
Let's think!
After all, a human came up with these questions!

1561
00:55:34,776 --> 00:55:38,376
[After a line right out of a shonen manga,
he sprints off]

1562
00:55:39,692 --> 00:55:40,817
Right now…

1563
00:55:40,817 --> 00:55:42,219
Oh!

1564
00:55:42,219 --> 00:55:44,386
I got it!
I just need to find them now!

1565
00:55:47,376 --> 00:55:49,709
I need to find this…
I'm sure it's here…

1566
00:55:53,943 --> 00:55:59,043
[The area where Yo Han
and DAWN spotted the eagle earlier]

1567
00:56:01,309 --> 00:56:03,143
What is this?

1568
00:56:03,143 --> 00:56:04,377
Oh?!

1569
00:56:04,377 --> 00:56:06,343
Here it is!

1570
00:56:06,343 --> 00:56:10,576
It's this! It's this kind of thing!

1571
00:56:11,276 --> 00:56:13,510
Yeah, it's finding the letters.

1572
00:56:13,510 --> 00:56:15,156
[Lee Teuk Collection Status: A]
"A".

1573
00:56:15,156 --> 00:56:16,610
Oh, okay!

1574
00:56:17,409 --> 00:56:21,109
I have been really bad at these things
since I was a kid.

1575
00:56:22,054 --> 00:56:25,244
Everyone, no matter what you're doing,

1576
00:56:25,244 --> 00:56:28,943
take a moment
to look out at the sea...!

1577
00:56:28,943 --> 00:56:32,209
[Immersed in the ocean view]

1578
00:56:33,671 --> 00:56:37,543
What are we supposed to find?

1579
00:56:41,976 --> 00:56:44,276
Wow. This place is amazing!

1580
00:56:46,043 --> 00:56:48,843
[Collecting romance instead of hieroglyphics...]

1581
00:56:49,443 --> 00:56:52,676
[Johnny can't resist
a heart-shaped decoration]

1582
00:56:53,709 --> 00:56:56,276
[Is this right...]

1583
00:56:57,009 --> 00:56:59,876
No way it's here.

1584
00:57:00,309 --> 00:57:03,067
Come down carefully now.

1585
00:57:03,067 --> 00:57:06,069
[Starting to search near the parasol]
Things like this are suspicious.

1586
00:57:06,069 --> 00:57:07,770
It's nothing at all.

1587
00:57:08,491 --> 00:57:10,809
Then what needs to be here?

1588
00:57:15,343 --> 00:57:18,178
Do I have to check inside each one?

1589
00:57:18,178 --> 00:57:19,509
Wow!

1590
00:57:19,509 --> 00:57:22,976
[Lucky enough to spot
the owl drawing right away!]

1591
00:57:26,069 --> 00:57:28,064
When I finally found one,

1592
00:57:28,064 --> 00:57:30,643
"Oh! This is what it is!"

1593
00:57:30,643 --> 00:57:33,110
It was hidden really deep.

1594
00:57:33,110 --> 00:57:36,109
I had to look closely to find it.

1595
00:57:36,109 --> 00:57:37,844
So, slowly and thoroughly!

1596
00:57:37,844 --> 00:57:39,476
If I'm looking at it,
let me get a proper look!

1597
00:57:39,476 --> 00:57:41,676
[Johnny's Collection Status: M]

1598
00:57:41,676 --> 00:57:44,876
So I have to check each and every one.

1599
00:57:50,309 --> 00:57:53,409
[Charming Chicago hot guy]

1600
00:57:54,776 --> 00:57:57,876
[Checking each one meticulously]

1601
00:57:57,876 --> 00:57:58,777
Isn't this over the top?

1602
00:57:58,777 --> 00:58:00,676
I'm going overboard
doing it like this, right?

1603
00:58:00,676 --> 00:58:03,376
[The Search Hamster
is still scurrying about]

1604
00:58:03,943 --> 00:58:06,677
[Trait 1: Answers immediately when asked]

1605
00:58:06,677 --> 00:58:09,309
[Trait 2: If you suggest sharing,
he only gives his own letters and leaves]

1606
00:58:09,309 --> 00:58:12,976
Oh, I'm tired...

1607
00:58:15,509 --> 00:58:17,277
[Found a spaceship-shaped hieroglyph]

1608
00:58:17,277 --> 00:58:19,005
What is the UFO? UFO.

1609
00:58:19,743 --> 00:58:20,677
M, R.

1610
00:58:20,677 --> 00:58:22,676
A, L, M, R.

1611
00:58:22,676 --> 00:58:24,561
A, L, M, R.

1612
00:58:25,443 --> 00:58:27,909
Let's take it step by step.

1613
00:58:27,909 --> 00:58:29,582
[DAWN's Collection Status: A]
"The one who finds and understands the ancient language…"

1614
00:58:29,582 --> 00:58:31,054
[The ancient language…]

1615
00:58:34,743 --> 00:58:36,476
Ji Sung!

1616
00:58:36,476 --> 00:58:37,776
Ji Sung!!!

1617
00:58:37,776 --> 00:58:40,344
I wish they'd tell us
how many clues there are.

1618
00:58:40,344 --> 00:58:41,544
How many did you find?

1619
00:58:41,544 --> 00:58:42,677
(Smirk)

1620
00:58:42,677 --> 00:58:43,677
4.

1621
00:58:43,677 --> 00:58:44,923
- You found 4?
- Yeah.

1622
00:58:44,923 --> 00:58:46,376
- For real?
- Yeah.

1623
00:58:46,376 --> 00:58:47,876
[Pure curiosity]
Where on earth did you find them?

1624
00:58:48,867 --> 00:58:50,580
[While DAWN found one,]
Why am I the only one who can't find it?

1625
00:58:50,580 --> 00:58:52,503
[Ji Sung found 4]
Did we not check over there?

1626
00:58:53,476 --> 00:58:54,909
Did I really not go there?

1627
00:58:55,776 --> 00:58:58,376
[Ji Sung runs again]

1628
00:59:04,843 --> 00:59:07,343
I don't think I've been here yet!

1629
00:59:10,109 --> 00:59:13,077
There's no guarantee
that it's even hanging here.

1630
00:59:13,077 --> 00:59:15,743
[Meticulous]
I gotta check the floor carefully too.

1631
00:59:16,176 --> 00:59:17,884
Oh, I have been here before!
Dang it.

1632
00:59:17,884 --> 00:59:20,276
Ugh, this is exhausting...

1633
00:59:20,276 --> 00:59:21,809
Huh?

1634
00:59:22,343 --> 00:59:25,312
[Found the cane drawing]

1635
00:59:25,312 --> 00:59:29,670
[Found a 'C']
A, L, M, R, C.

1636
00:59:29,670 --> 00:59:32,007
[Found 5 in total]
A, L, M, R, C.

1637
00:59:32,007 --> 00:59:33,960
A, L, M, R, C.

1638
00:59:34,943 --> 00:59:35,877
[Current Letter Collection Status]

1639
00:59:35,877 --> 00:59:37,278
[1st place: Ji Sung]
[2nd place: Yo Han]

1640
00:59:37,278 --> 00:59:38,777
[Tied for 3rd]
[Johnny / DAWN / Lee Teuk]

1641
00:59:38,777 --> 00:59:39,709
[6th place: Shin Dong]

1642
00:59:40,443 --> 00:59:42,177
Why aren't you moving?

1643
00:59:42,177 --> 00:59:44,077
I have to find at least one thing,

1644
00:59:44,077 --> 00:59:47,443
[Downcast]
but I couldn't find a single thing...

1645
00:59:48,176 --> 00:59:50,087
[Never-ending]
"A big pool of fresh water…"

1646
00:59:50,087 --> 00:59:52,068
[Forever trapped in the freshwater pool hell]

1647
00:59:52,068 --> 00:59:54,476
This really looks like a clue.

1648
00:59:57,369 --> 01:00:00,777
Ji Sung, sorry,
but can I ask you something?

1649
01:00:00,777 --> 01:00:02,710
Are the clues written on paper?

1650
01:00:02,710 --> 01:00:04,277
- Yeah, they're on paper.
- Oh.

1651
01:00:04,277 --> 01:00:05,445
[Shin Dong hasn't seen the ancient language yet]
I haven't found a single one.

1652
01:00:05,445 --> 01:00:07,380
So you look at it
and then copy it here?

1653
01:00:07,380 --> 01:00:09,842
Rather than writing it down,
you can just remember it.

1654
01:00:09,842 --> 01:00:11,944
- How many did you find?
- 5.

1655
01:00:11,944 --> 01:00:13,177
You found 5?

1656
01:00:13,177 --> 01:00:14,177
There are 5?

1657
01:00:14,177 --> 01:00:15,584
Ji Sung, want to share?

1658
01:00:15,584 --> 01:00:17,376
I'll solve the puzzle for you.

1659
01:00:17,376 --> 01:00:18,910
How's that sound?

1660
01:00:18,910 --> 01:00:21,029
[Proposing an investigative alliance]
I haven't found a single clue so far.

1661
01:00:21,029 --> 01:00:22,784
- Really?
- Yeah.

1662
01:00:22,784 --> 01:00:24,786
- Then I'll come find you again later.
- Oh, okay, okay.

1663
01:00:24,786 --> 01:00:25,765
(100% on guard)

1664
01:00:25,765 --> 01:00:29,036
If you've got five,
I think we can crack the answer.

1665
01:00:29,036 --> 01:00:30,609
That's right.

1666
01:00:30,609 --> 01:00:32,144
Ji Sung, think it through carefully.

1667
01:00:32,144 --> 01:00:33,977
[Coaxing him]
You gotta hurry and become a prince.

1668
01:00:33,977 --> 01:00:36,877
Let me find just one more clue,
and I'll come find you!

1669
01:00:36,877 --> 01:00:38,743
How did he find those clues?

1670
01:00:39,976 --> 01:00:42,576
I'm taking it all for myself!

1671
01:00:43,176 --> 01:00:46,776
[Ancient language]
5...?

1672
01:00:46,776 --> 01:00:50,076
[Still only found one]
I'm the only one who can't find anything!

1673
01:00:51,409 --> 01:00:52,843
[Swish]

1674
01:01:00,269 --> 01:01:03,676
[DAWN discovers his second hieroglyphic]

1675
01:01:04,336 --> 01:01:07,381
[The letter this image points to is]

1676
01:01:07,381 --> 01:01:08,277
Y.

1677
01:01:08,277 --> 01:01:09,877
["E/Y" acquired]
[DAWN's Collection Status: A, EY]

1678
01:01:09,877 --> 01:01:11,079
Ey…

1679
01:01:11,878 --> 01:01:13,580
[E... Y... Why are there 2 of them?]

1680
01:01:13,580 --> 01:01:14,883
Ey…

1681
01:01:16,209 --> 01:01:17,177
[DAWN's Collection Status: A, EY]

1682
01:01:17,177 --> 01:01:17,777
A.

1683
01:01:17,777 --> 01:01:19,051
Ey, A.

1684
01:01:20,843 --> 01:01:25,943
[Could it be hidden in the Red Sea?]

1685
01:01:26,376 --> 01:01:30,643
[Now everyone's looking through the parasols]

1686
01:01:30,643 --> 01:01:34,810
[Folding himself down
to a third of his size to search]

1687
